WEBVTT

1
00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:25.917
["Love the Way" playing]

2
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.875
[woman imitating drumroll] <i>Ta-da!</i>

3
00:00:29.375 --> 00:00:31.833
<i>The Amur Adonis buds
have finally sprouted.</i>

4
00:00:31.917 --> 00:00:34.000
- [man 1] <i>Lift that up a bit more.</i>
- [woman laughs]

5
00:00:34.083 --> 00:00:38.625
<i>Today marks a momentous day as life has
once again sprouted from this red soil.</i>

6
00:00:38.708 --> 00:00:41.667
<i>Okay, I guess it technically didn't sprout
from the soil.</i>

7
00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.417
[man 1] <i>Santa's unaffected by gravity.</i>

8
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.292
[man 2] <i>Uh, that's debatable.</i>

9
00:00:45.375 --> 00:00:49.000
<i>I say Santa's affected by the gravity,
but Rudolph and the sleigh aren't.</i>

10
00:00:50.375 --> 00:00:52.375
<i>Aren't you guys putting
too much effort into this?</i>

11
00:00:52.458 --> 00:00:55.917
<i>I wish you had that level of enthusiasm
for analyzing soil samples.</i>

12
00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:57.500
[man 2] <i>Seriously?</i>

13
00:00:58.833 --> 00:01:02.500
<i>Ji-young, another video journal
to your daughter, hmm?</i>

14
00:01:03.375 --> 00:01:06.458
<i>Hi, Nan-young.
I heard you got another rotten tooth.</i>

15
00:01:06.542 --> 00:01:09.083
<i>The news of that even reached Mars.</i>

16
00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:12.083
- [panicked talking]
- [woman 2] <i>Stay calm!</i>

17
00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:14.375
<i>Head to the emergency exit!</i>

18
00:01:14.458 --> 00:01:16.542
- [man 2] <i>Hurry!</i>
- [woman 2] <i>Ji-young!</i>

19
00:01:16.625 --> 00:01:17.792
[dramatic sting]

20
00:01:18.917 --> 00:01:19.750
[radio crackles]

21
00:01:19.833 --> 00:01:22.708
HQ? Joo here.
I'm in the habitat module now.

22
00:01:22.792 --> 00:01:25.167
[NASA officer] <i>Copy.</i>
<i>Proceed slowly and steadily.</i>

23
00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:28.167
<i>- Your pace is good.</i>
- Heading towards ISRU for supplies.

24
00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:29.458
[beeping]

25
00:01:29.542 --> 00:01:30.833
[rustling]

26
00:01:30.917 --> 00:01:31.917
[grunts]

27
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.833
Suit, display
the oxygen generator location.

28
00:01:34.917 --> 00:01:36.958
[breathing heavily]

29
00:01:37.042 --> 00:01:39.042
[metal creaking]

30
00:01:41.125 --> 00:01:43.833
[grunting]

31
00:01:43.917 --> 00:01:45.208
Oxygen tank secured.

32
00:01:45.792 --> 00:01:46.792
[grunts]

33
00:01:47.792 --> 00:01:48.667
[grunts]

34
00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:50.167
Initiating recharge.

35
00:01:54.833 --> 00:01:56.167
[grunts]

36
00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:58.250
[intriguing music playing]

37
00:02:00.292 --> 00:02:01.292
[grunts]

38
00:02:05.292 --> 00:02:07.792
[dramatic sting]

39
00:02:07.875 --> 00:02:09.875
[surreal music playing]

40
00:02:12.458 --> 00:02:14.750
[music builds]

41
00:02:15.333 --> 00:02:17.083
[heavy breathing]

42
00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:19.000
[NASA officer] <i>Nan-young,</i>
<i>what's the holdup?</i>

43
00:02:19.083 --> 00:02:21.375
<i>- Recharge now.</i>
- [Nan-young gasping]

44
00:02:21.458 --> 00:02:24.125
- [breathing heavily, gasps]
- [oxygen hisses]

45
00:02:24.208 --> 00:02:26.089
- [researcher 1] <i>Nailed it!</i>
- [researcher 2] <i>Done.</i>

46
00:02:26.125 --> 00:02:28.792
[researcher 1] <i>She's practically built</i>
<i>for Mars missions.</i>

47
00:02:29.375 --> 00:02:31.958
- [researcher 2] <i>All right. That's a wrap.</i>
- [researcher 1] <i>I know!</i>

48
00:02:32.042 --> 00:02:34.708
Without that tiny stall,
it would've been a record.

49
00:02:34.792 --> 00:02:37.000
- Why'd you stop?
- [Nan-young] I thought I saw something.

50
00:02:37.083 --> 00:02:39.167
Really? I'll look at it.

51
00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:42.167
- Ready to call it a day?
- Yep. Let's get out of here.

52
00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:44.708
[man] Oh, Sam, by the way,
the engineers requested a meeting

53
00:02:44.792 --> 00:02:47.208
about the rotation axis issue
from the last gravity test.

54
00:02:49.292 --> 00:02:54.000
I cannot accept this decision.
There were no issues with my test results.

55
00:02:54.083 --> 00:02:56.250
The bereaved families
received their belongings,

56
00:02:56.333 --> 00:02:59.167
and as you can imagine,
old wounds are reopening.

57
00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:01.833
You're the only member of
the Mars Expedition crew

58
00:03:01.917 --> 00:03:03.167
who lost someone.

59
00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:05.625
It's just too cruel for you to visit
the accident site

60
00:03:05.708 --> 00:03:07.000
during this mission.

61
00:03:07.083 --> 00:03:08.292
[Nan-young scoffs]

62
00:03:08.875 --> 00:03:10.792
You know what's really cruel, Captain?

63
00:03:11.458 --> 00:03:14.417
You know how much work I put into this.

64
00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:16.292
I swear, I'm not affected.

65
00:03:17.458 --> 00:03:19.167
You're really not affected?

66
00:03:19.708 --> 00:03:22.500
[sighs] That's exactly the problem.

67
00:03:22.583 --> 00:03:26.417
See, Nan-young, that's not
a normal psychological response.

68
00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:30.500
The doctor expressed concerns
about that aspect of your psyche.

69
00:03:31.333 --> 00:03:33.042
Stand by as a backup for now.

70
00:03:33.583 --> 00:03:36.292
Why don't you have a little break
in Korea? Clear your head.

71
00:03:43.708 --> 00:03:44.833
[reporter] <i>Breaking news.</i>

72
00:03:44.917 --> 00:03:46.458
<i>As the astronaut selection process</i>

73
00:03:46.542 --> 00:03:49.583
<i>for the upcoming fourth Mars expedition
has officially begun,</i>

74
00:03:49.667 --> 00:03:52.667
<i>NASA is now able to share more details
about the mission.</i>

75
00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:55.667
<i>Twenty-four years ago,
a large tremor on the surface of Mars</i>

76
00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:59.250
<i>caused the collapse of
an underground manned research facility.</i>

77
00:03:59.333 --> 00:04:03.375
<i>All crew members of the second Mars
expedition were lost in this tragedy.</i>

78
00:04:03.458 --> 00:04:07.000
<i>The incident was devastating,
not only for the families of the lost crew</i>

79
00:04:07.083 --> 00:04:10.042
<i>but also for the people of the world
who had collectively hoped</i>

80
00:04:10.125 --> 00:04:11.333
<i>for their safe return.</i>

81
00:04:11.833 --> 00:04:13.750
<i>The belongings of the late Son Ji-young,</i>

82
00:04:13.833 --> 00:04:17.000
<i>the first Korean astronaut selected
for a Mars expedition,</i>

83
00:04:17.083 --> 00:04:19.917
<i>will be among the items brought back
from the red planet.</i>

84
00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.583
[poignant music playing]

85
00:04:27.833 --> 00:04:28.875
[quirky music playing]

86
00:04:28.958 --> 00:04:31.208
[announcer] <i>Seoul Station Square</i>
<i>and surrounding zones</i>

87
00:04:31.292 --> 00:04:33.375
<i>are approved for low-flying drones.</i>

88
00:04:33.458 --> 00:04:37.833
<i>Air taxi drivers are advised to exercise
caution and avoid drone collisions.</i>

89
00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:39.750
<i>Once again…</i>

90
00:04:42.917 --> 00:04:43.917
[sighs]

91
00:04:45.625 --> 00:04:46.625
[mellow music plays]

92
00:04:46.708 --> 00:04:48.750
- [sighs]
- [ringtone]

93
00:04:48.833 --> 00:04:51.083
- [Rosa] <i>Hey, Nans! Did you get home safe?</i>
- You scared me!

94
00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:54.000
- [Rosa] <i>How are you feeling?</i>
- How am I feeling?

95
00:04:54.583 --> 00:04:57.917
Oh, I feel like I'm watching my dreams
crumble before my eyes.

96
00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:59.000
[Rosa] <i>Aw.</i>

97
00:04:59.333 --> 00:05:01.875
<i>Come on. Let me see your face.
Turn on your camera.</i>

98
00:05:02.583 --> 00:05:05.792
- Fine. Here's my crestfallen face.
- [Rosa] <i>Hmm.</i>

99
00:05:06.417 --> 00:05:07.667
[Rosa laughs]

100
00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:10.500
<i>Whoa! What, do you live
in some antique store?</i>

101
00:05:10.583 --> 00:05:12.542
<i>Where did you get it all?</i>

102
00:05:12.625 --> 00:05:14.333
It's Mom and Dad's.

103
00:05:14.417 --> 00:05:16.958
Uh, I really need to go through it all
one of these days.

104
00:05:17.042 --> 00:05:19.500
<i>Oh my gosh. This is so dang cute!</i>

105
00:05:19.583 --> 00:05:21.042
Hey!

106
00:05:21.125 --> 00:05:23.042
- Quit walking through me!
- [detector] <i>Scanning.</i>

107
00:05:23.125 --> 00:05:24.292
[Rosa] <i>Excuse you!</i>

108
00:05:24.375 --> 00:05:27.143
- [Nan-young] Stop getting in my way.
- [detector] <i>Target. Managing mode.</i>

109
00:05:27.167 --> 00:05:31.083
- [grunts] Move it.
<i>- Whoa! Hey! Hey! </i>[Groans]

110
00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:34.667
- [giggles]
- [detector trills]

111
00:05:35.458 --> 00:05:38.333
[gasps]

112
00:05:38.417 --> 00:05:40.292
[Rosa] <i>Whoa!</i>

113
00:05:42.417 --> 00:05:44.542
- Hey!
<i>- Bye, Nans. Talk soon!</i>

114
00:05:44.625 --> 00:05:46.875
- [Nan-young moans]
- [detector beeping]

115
00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:51.750
[quirky music playing]

116
00:06:26.917 --> 00:06:30.292
LOST IN STARLIGHT

117
00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:46.458
MARS EXPEDITION TEAM'S BELONGINGS RETURN
AFTER 25 YEARS

118
00:06:46.542 --> 00:06:51.708
MODERN ELECTRONICS REPAIRS

119
00:06:58.167 --> 00:07:00.500
[both gasp]

120
00:07:04.958 --> 00:07:06.958
[cries out]

121
00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:09.042
[gasps]

122
00:07:15.917 --> 00:07:17.667
[music builds, ends]

123
00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:19.375
[both gasp]

124
00:07:20.208 --> 00:07:23.667
- [man] Oh, I'm so sorry. Are you okay?
- [Nan-young gasps]

125
00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:25.875
[breathing heavily]

126
00:07:25.958 --> 00:07:27.833
- That was totally my fault.
- [beeping]

127
00:07:27.917 --> 00:07:30.875
[man on smart watch] <i>Hey, hurry it up</i>
<i>and get over here. </i>[Laughs]

128
00:07:31.458 --> 00:07:33.958
<i>Oh boy, look at him. Ah.</i>

129
00:07:34.042 --> 00:07:35.167
Oh, I'm late.

130
00:07:35.667 --> 00:07:37.333
[Nan-young] Uh, you should get going.

131
00:07:37.833 --> 00:07:38.833
Huh?

132
00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:40.750
[Nan-young] Oh…

133
00:07:41.667 --> 00:07:44.208
The Crozley All-in-one 2023 edition?

134
00:07:44.708 --> 00:07:47.458
I can, uh, repair that for you. [Chuckles]

135
00:07:47.542 --> 00:07:49.917
- Uh...
- Here's my card. Bring it by.

136
00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:51.625
I'll fix it for you.

137
00:07:51.708 --> 00:07:54.083
- So sorry!
- Wait! Uh…

138
00:07:55.792 --> 00:07:58.208
- That one's for unit 402.
- 402?

139
00:07:58.292 --> 00:08:00.052
Just send it up there.
They'll figure it out.

140
00:08:00.083 --> 00:08:02.250
- Right. Have a good day.
- [Nan-young] Hmm.

141
00:08:02.333 --> 00:08:03.333
[whirring]

142
00:08:03.375 --> 00:08:05.375
[man panting]

143
00:08:09.542 --> 00:08:11.542
[people chattering]

144
00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:22.417
[man] Ah, come on.
I just had it a second ago. Where did it...

145
00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:24.667
- ♪ <i>I've been looking for love… </i> ♪
- Huh.

146
00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:26.670
[man] I know I had
the soldering iron right here.

147
00:08:28.083 --> 00:08:29.167
Ah, there it is.

148
00:08:30.625 --> 00:08:32.292
Let's have a look now, shall we?

149
00:08:34.083 --> 00:08:35.125
Huh.

150
00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:38.333
[woman] I brought this to you
over a month ago,

151
00:08:38.417 --> 00:08:40.417
and you're just now taking a look at it?

152
00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:43.417
[man] Well, see, Jay said
that he had already finished it...

153
00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:45.625
[woman] Indispensable employee, isn't he?

154
00:08:45.708 --> 00:08:48.208
Without him, there'd be no one
to pin the blame on.

155
00:08:48.292 --> 00:08:50.250
All right. I'm working. Don't distract me.

156
00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:52.125
[Nan-young grunts]

157
00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:54.125
So…

158
00:08:55.833 --> 00:08:58.958
There is a young guy
that works here, right?

159
00:08:59.625 --> 00:09:01.083
- Young guy?
- [Nan-young] Yeah.

160
00:09:01.708 --> 00:09:03.917
Hmm. Oh, Jay.

161
00:09:04.417 --> 00:09:05.417
Hey, Jay.

162
00:09:05.917 --> 00:09:08.792
- [Jay] Oh, you came.
- Oh, Jay!

163
00:09:08.875 --> 00:09:10.667
- Who's she?
- Girlfriend?

164
00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:12.542
Oh, uh. Come on, Miss Oh.

165
00:09:12.625 --> 00:09:14.042
- I, uh…
- [Miss Oh laughs]

166
00:09:14.125 --> 00:09:15.125
She's a customer.

167
00:09:15.167 --> 00:09:17.708
- [Miss Oh] Goodness, me.
- [man] Oh, to be young again…

168
00:09:17.792 --> 00:09:19.625
- Pipe down.
- [Miss Oh] Time of your life.

169
00:09:19.708 --> 00:09:22.875
- [Jay] Do you want me to load them?
- Ah, you take care of your customer.

170
00:09:22.958 --> 00:09:24.500
- Okay.
- Nice work, Jay.

171
00:09:24.583 --> 00:09:25.750
Thank you, Miss Oh.

172
00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:27.292
Uh, follow me.

173
00:09:28.083 --> 00:09:30.083
- Uh, this way.
- [Nan-young] Mm.

174
00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:33.708
Glad you were able to find the place okay.

175
00:09:33.792 --> 00:09:36.125
I was worried you might not
since I rushed off.

176
00:09:36.208 --> 00:09:37.750
- Come on up.
- Oh, sure.

177
00:09:37.833 --> 00:09:38.833
- Hmm.
- [Jay sighs]

178
00:09:38.875 --> 00:09:42.167
SEWOON PLAZA

179
00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:44.250
[piano music playing]

180
00:09:44.958 --> 00:09:46.042
Uh…

181
00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:47.750
Hmm.

182
00:09:50.083 --> 00:09:52.208
The board right here is smashed.

183
00:09:53.208 --> 00:09:54.333
Yeah, thanks to you.

184
00:09:54.417 --> 00:09:57.875
I doubt it was in working condition
before it took that little tumble.

185
00:09:57.958 --> 00:09:59.333
- [Nan-young] Mm-mm.
- [Jay] Hmm.

186
00:10:00.333 --> 00:10:02.792
So, do you really think you can fix it?

187
00:10:02.875 --> 00:10:05.083
Well, I'll try to start sourcing
the parts.

188
00:10:05.167 --> 00:10:08.667
Between my connections
and the fact this is a budget retro item,

189
00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:09.750
shouldn't take long.

190
00:10:10.792 --> 00:10:11.792
Hmm?

191
00:10:12.167 --> 00:10:14.000
Can I get your name and number?

192
00:10:15.583 --> 00:10:16.792
[Nan-young] Uh.

193
00:10:18.042 --> 00:10:19.958
- Hmm.
- Hmm.

194
00:10:20.042 --> 00:10:22.250
I'll give you a call
as soon as it's ready.

195
00:10:23.958 --> 00:10:25.625
- Here.
- [Nan-young] Uh…

196
00:10:25.708 --> 00:10:26.750
[Jay] You click it.

197
00:10:26.833 --> 00:10:27.833
Oh.

198
00:10:30.083 --> 00:10:32.125
JOO NAN-YOUNG

199
00:10:32.208 --> 00:10:33.458
[Rosa] <i>With a pen? On paper?</i>

200
00:10:34.167 --> 00:10:37.292
<i>Wow. Those guys still exist?</i>

201
00:10:37.875 --> 00:10:40.583
<i>Hey! This is a perfect opportunity
to clear your head.</i>

202
00:10:40.667 --> 00:10:41.833
<i>You should set up a date.</i>

203
00:10:41.917 --> 00:10:42.958
Chill.

204
00:10:43.042 --> 00:10:45.625
How are things going at the lab?
And with the board?

205
00:10:45.708 --> 00:10:46.708
[Rosa] <i>Mm.</i>

206
00:10:47.458 --> 00:10:50.833
<i>Well, your psych test scores
have barely made the cut,</i>

207
00:10:50.917 --> 00:10:54.708
<i>but you can probably make it up elsewhere.
Look at this.</i>

208
00:10:54.792 --> 00:10:56.917
Rosa, what did you find for me?

209
00:10:57.417 --> 00:10:59.375
<i>You can see
they've encountered some issues</i>

210
00:10:59.458 --> 00:11:01.917
<i>with the atomic battery
on the life detector.</i>

211
00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:04.875
Let's see.
I need to get it from 270 to 300?

212
00:11:06.417 --> 00:11:09.875
<i>It's obvious the team
has really been struggling since you left.</i>

213
00:11:09.958 --> 00:11:10.958
Hmm.

214
00:11:12.458 --> 00:11:13.375
Okay.

215
00:11:13.458 --> 00:11:15.292
I gotta stay on top of my game.

216
00:11:15.375 --> 00:11:18.500
Inspiration might strike at any moment,
you know?

217
00:11:18.583 --> 00:11:19.983
DR. JOO NAN-YOUNG DEMOTED TO BACKUP

218
00:11:20.042 --> 00:11:22.833
Absolutely. Let me know if you find
anything in similar condition.

219
00:11:22.917 --> 00:11:25.250
- [merchant] Will do. Later.
- We'll be on our way. Thanks!

220
00:11:26.625 --> 00:11:29.125
I'm gonna sit as far from the teachers
as I can.

221
00:11:29.208 --> 00:11:31.042
[boy] You were up all night practicing?

222
00:11:31.125 --> 00:11:33.208
Don't tell me you've given up
on music completely.

223
00:11:33.292 --> 00:11:35.042
You wanna end up like me?

224
00:11:35.125 --> 00:11:37.250
[Jay scoffs] Come on now.

225
00:11:38.083 --> 00:11:40.083
What would be so bad
about ending up like you?

226
00:11:40.167 --> 00:11:42.250
[Jay's boss] Uh, you're nuts,
you know that?

227
00:11:43.667 --> 00:11:44.708
[Jay] Oh.

228
00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:47.333
Oh!

229
00:11:47.417 --> 00:11:48.667
DR. JOO NAN-YOUNG

230
00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:50.458
Wait. She's a famous person?

231
00:11:50.542 --> 00:11:52.417
[Jay's boss] What's grabbed
your attention now?

232
00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:53.500
[Jay chuckles]

233
00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:55.625
I'm so impressed.

234
00:11:57.250 --> 00:11:58.083
Hmm.

235
00:11:58.167 --> 00:12:00.167
["Life Goes On" playing]

236
00:12:03.333 --> 00:12:04.333
[sighs]

237
00:12:08.417 --> 00:12:10.417
Do we have the noise test results yet?

238
00:12:12.917 --> 00:12:14.597
[researcher] I'm out of here
for the night.

239
00:12:17.833 --> 00:12:22.125
<i>♪ I wake up from my bed ♪</i>

240
00:12:22.208 --> 00:12:25.750
♪ <i>Just to find it was a dream </i> ♪

241
00:12:26.375 --> 00:12:30.458
♪ <i>Is it my darkest fear? </i> ♪

242
00:12:30.542 --> 00:12:34.542
♪ <i>No one will be there for me </i> ♪

243
00:12:34.625 --> 00:12:36.625
♪ <i>I do know </i> ♪

244
00:12:36.708 --> 00:12:38.875
- [song continues in Korean]
- Look!

245
00:12:39.375 --> 00:12:41.333
- [zapping]
- Oh!

246
00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:47.750
<i>Nan-young here.</i>

247
00:12:47.792 --> 00:12:50.333
<i>To address your concerns
and demonstrate my readiness,</i>

248
00:12:50.417 --> 00:12:52.750
<i>I've continued working on upgrading
the performance</i>

249
00:12:52.833 --> 00:12:54.833
<i>of the life-form detector
since returning home.</i>

250
00:12:55.417 --> 00:12:57.333
<i>The research
has been progressing smoothly,</i>

251
00:12:57.417 --> 00:12:59.958
<i>and I am on track to reach 300
prior to launch.</i>

252
00:13:00.042 --> 00:13:03.000
<i>If so, I am hopeful
that you will consider allowing me</i>

253
00:13:03.083 --> 00:13:04.667
<i>to lead the upcoming Mars expedition.</i>

254
00:13:04.750 --> 00:13:05.750
[sighs]

255
00:13:09.958 --> 00:13:11.500
[watch dings]

256
00:13:12.708 --> 00:13:14.208
[song fades]

257
00:13:14.292 --> 00:13:16.000
[Jay] <i>Good news!</i>

258
00:13:16.083 --> 00:13:18.750
<i>I think I have a solution.
Can we meet tomorrow?</i>

259
00:13:19.833 --> 00:13:22.083
[repairman] Oh dear, well…

260
00:13:22.167 --> 00:13:24.042
Looks like it's not a fit after all.

261
00:13:24.125 --> 00:13:26.625
- Sorry for making you waste a trip.
- [Jay] Uh…

262
00:13:27.208 --> 00:13:29.417
No problem.
Thanks for having a look at it.

263
00:13:31.708 --> 00:13:34.292
- [Jay sighs]
- Come on, just give it back.

264
00:13:34.375 --> 00:13:38.500
Ugh. I don't want to be a bother.
It's not that important anyway.

265
00:13:38.583 --> 00:13:40.667
- It's not even mine.
- Huh? What?

266
00:13:41.667 --> 00:13:44.292
But here. Scribbled right on the front.

267
00:13:44.375 --> 00:13:45.917
"Nan-young."

268
00:13:46.667 --> 00:13:47.833
That's not you?

269
00:13:48.625 --> 00:13:49.625
It is, but…

270
00:13:51.708 --> 00:13:52.750
It was my mom's.

271
00:13:53.750 --> 00:13:54.958
[Jay] Well, then.

272
00:13:55.042 --> 00:13:57.125
All the more reason to fix it.

273
00:13:57.208 --> 00:13:58.333
[Nan-young grunts]

274
00:13:58.417 --> 00:14:01.125
Listen, sir. I understand
you've already put a lot of work into it,

275
00:14:01.208 --> 00:14:02.792
but really, it's not a big deal.

276
00:14:03.292 --> 00:14:04.292
Um…

277
00:14:05.125 --> 00:14:07.375
You don't have to call me "sir." Just Jay.

278
00:14:07.458 --> 00:14:08.458
Huh?

279
00:14:08.792 --> 00:14:09.792
It's my name.

280
00:14:10.292 --> 00:14:11.333
Call me Jay.

281
00:14:11.833 --> 00:14:14.167
Okay then, Jay. [Laughs]

282
00:14:14.250 --> 00:14:16.958
- Well, thanks but... [gasps]
- I know!

283
00:14:17.042 --> 00:14:19.458
I've worked up quite the appetite.

284
00:14:19.958 --> 00:14:21.792
What do you say? Wanna grab a bite?

285
00:14:21.875 --> 00:14:23.167
[Jay chuckles]

286
00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:25.083
[sighs]

287
00:14:25.167 --> 00:14:27.333
[slurps] Oh!

288
00:14:27.417 --> 00:14:30.083
Never tastes this good
when I make it at home.

289
00:14:30.167 --> 00:14:32.417
They say food tastes better
when you're not the chef.

290
00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:33.750
But then again,

291
00:14:33.833 --> 00:14:36.875
they also say food tastes better
when enjoyed with… friends?

292
00:14:36.958 --> 00:14:38.667
- Oh, we're friends?
- [Jay chuckles]

293
00:14:39.583 --> 00:14:42.208
Just a turn of phrase, you know?

294
00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:44.667
Let me get the check.

295
00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:47.417
- It's the least I can do for you, sir.
- Come on now.

296
00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:50.708
Enough with the "sir." It's Jay.

297
00:14:50.792 --> 00:14:52.750
Let's just use our first names.

298
00:14:52.833 --> 00:14:54.713
After all, we have to see each other
three times

299
00:14:54.792 --> 00:14:57.833
so we can fix this bad boy. Right?

300
00:14:57.917 --> 00:14:59.875
- [Nan-young sighs] Then…
- Oh.

301
00:15:00.792 --> 00:15:03.042
Call me by my name the third time.

302
00:15:03.125 --> 00:15:05.542
[Jay] Oh, uh… don't be a stranger.

303
00:15:06.625 --> 00:15:07.792
Huh.

304
00:15:09.542 --> 00:15:10.542
Hmm.

305
00:15:12.958 --> 00:15:15.417
[thunder rumbling]

306
00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:16.875
[rain pattering]

307
00:15:17.958 --> 00:15:18.958
Huh?

308
00:15:19.625 --> 00:15:20.667
[sighs]

309
00:15:24.542 --> 00:15:25.875
- [horn honking]
- [exclaims]

310
00:15:25.958 --> 00:15:26.958
Uh!

311
00:15:27.458 --> 00:15:30.208
[grunting]

312
00:15:30.833 --> 00:15:33.125
[panting]

313
00:15:34.083 --> 00:15:35.083
Huh?

314
00:15:36.458 --> 00:15:37.458
Nan-young.

315
00:15:38.167 --> 00:15:39.167
Uh-huh?

316
00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:40.792
[whimsical music playing]

317
00:15:40.875 --> 00:15:42.167
[exhales]

318
00:15:43.125 --> 00:15:44.125
[sighs]

319
00:15:46.667 --> 00:15:48.917
- Uh.
- Oh.

320
00:15:50.833 --> 00:15:51.958
Oh.

321
00:15:52.542 --> 00:15:54.375
Well, this is our…

322
00:15:56.125 --> 00:15:59.750
Third time… meeting so…

323
00:16:00.833 --> 00:16:02.167
I can call you…

324
00:16:02.917 --> 00:16:04.000
[exhales]

325
00:16:04.083 --> 00:16:05.833
…by your name now, right?

326
00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:07.583
[Nan-young murmurs]

327
00:16:07.667 --> 00:16:09.833
[Jay pants]

328
00:16:09.917 --> 00:16:13.167
- Let me catch my breath.
- [Nan-young laughs]

329
00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:15.167
[both laugh]

330
00:16:16.917 --> 00:16:18.917
[music continues]

331
00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:26.500
- [Nan-young] Come on. Let's go.
- Okay. Here.

332
00:16:26.583 --> 00:16:28.458
How did you know
I didn't have an umbrella?

333
00:16:28.542 --> 00:16:32.125
You weren't carrying one earlier,
so I ran to catch up with you.

334
00:16:32.208 --> 00:16:34.125
[Nan-young laughs]

335
00:16:34.625 --> 00:16:35.833
[music fades]

336
00:16:39.042 --> 00:16:41.292
This is the model
that was released right after yours,

337
00:16:41.375 --> 00:16:44.042
but the specs and design
are basically the same.

338
00:16:45.292 --> 00:16:46.125
[Nan-young] Hmm.

339
00:16:46.208 --> 00:16:48.792
It wasn't exactly easy to get my hands on,

340
00:16:48.875 --> 00:16:52.292
but with my connections,
I was able to get it for pretty cheap.

341
00:16:52.792 --> 00:16:55.000
They look just about the same, don't they?

342
00:16:56.042 --> 00:16:57.208
What do you think?

343
00:16:57.292 --> 00:16:59.458
- It plays music?
- Of course.

344
00:16:59.542 --> 00:17:00.792
Let's put something on.

345
00:17:01.292 --> 00:17:02.292
Just a sec.

346
00:17:03.458 --> 00:17:04.458
Hmm.

347
00:17:06.833 --> 00:17:07.667
[watch chimes]

348
00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:09.833
[watch voice] <i>Bluetooth device connected.</i>

349
00:17:09.917 --> 00:17:10.917
Huh?

350
00:17:12.208 --> 00:17:13.917
We've got a functioning turntable,

351
00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:16.208
and you're using it
as a Bluetooth speaker?

352
00:17:16.875 --> 00:17:18.500
So trapped in the modern age.

353
00:17:18.583 --> 00:17:20.583
[mellow music begins]

354
00:17:20.667 --> 00:17:21.833
Uh…

355
00:17:22.833 --> 00:17:23.833
Oh.

356
00:17:24.417 --> 00:17:25.792
[sighs]

357
00:17:25.875 --> 00:17:27.458
My favorite song.

358
00:17:28.125 --> 00:17:30.333
I found it on cloud a few years ago
and was hooked.

359
00:17:30.917 --> 00:17:33.542
I think it's a demo of some kind.
Seems unfinished.

360
00:17:33.625 --> 00:17:35.625
<i>♪ I lose myself to fun… ♪</i>

361
00:17:36.125 --> 00:17:37.583
[Jay breathes shakily] Oh.

362
00:17:37.667 --> 00:17:40.583
I played this song over and over
while studying.

363
00:17:40.667 --> 00:17:42.792
My roommate couldn't take it
and moved out.

364
00:17:43.333 --> 00:17:45.000
[laughs] Funny, right?

365
00:17:45.625 --> 00:17:47.333
- [Jay] I can't believe it.
- Huh?

366
00:17:48.292 --> 00:17:50.458
[gasps] Do you know this track?

367
00:17:51.208 --> 00:17:54.250
- [Jay clears throat]
- [Nan-young laughs] That's wild!

368
00:17:54.333 --> 00:17:56.174
I've never met anyone else
who knows this song.

369
00:17:56.208 --> 00:17:59.000
Hmm. Yeah, it's wild.

370
00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:01.292
I deleted it right after posting.

371
00:18:02.750 --> 00:18:05.583
I never thought anyone
would actually hear it.

372
00:18:07.583 --> 00:18:08.583
Huh?

373
00:18:09.167 --> 00:18:10.750
This is your song?

374
00:18:11.292 --> 00:18:12.875
As in, you sang it?

375
00:18:14.208 --> 00:18:16.083
- You're lying! [Gasps]
- [bang]

376
00:18:16.167 --> 00:18:18.292
[Jay's boss] Our Jay here?
He never lies, I tell you.

377
00:18:18.375 --> 00:18:19.583
Oh, come on! Right now?

378
00:18:19.667 --> 00:18:23.625
I got no customers up there.
My part-timer is slacking off as usual.

379
00:18:23.708 --> 00:18:25.629
- Hey, I'm not slacking off.
- All in my way again.

380
00:18:25.708 --> 00:18:26.708
My guitar! Hey!

381
00:18:27.208 --> 00:18:28.208
- Sorry.
- [Jay] Oh!

382
00:18:28.792 --> 00:18:31.417
Stop using this space for naps! Ugh.

383
00:18:34.375 --> 00:18:35.750
[tuning guitar]

384
00:18:40.833 --> 00:18:41.958
Actually…

385
00:18:42.917 --> 00:18:45.750
It's still… pretty unfinished.

386
00:18:46.417 --> 00:18:47.833
Sure you wanna hear it?

387
00:18:47.917 --> 00:18:49.750
Uh, mm-hmm.

388
00:18:52.417 --> 00:18:53.458
[clears throat]

389
00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:56.125
[sighs]

390
00:18:56.708 --> 00:18:58.708
[strums guitar, stops]

391
00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:01.083
[exhales, strums guitar, stops]

392
00:19:01.667 --> 00:19:03.000
Three, four…

393
00:19:04.292 --> 00:19:07.125
♪ <i>I lose myself to fun </i> ♪

394
00:19:11.167 --> 00:19:14.083
♪ <i>In nameless cities </i> ♪

395
00:19:14.167 --> 00:19:17.375
<i>♪ Drifting to the unknown ♪</i>

396
00:19:22.708 --> 00:19:26.000
♪ <i>Sleeping somewhere in between ♪</i>

397
00:19:26.083 --> 00:19:33.042
<i>♪ For someone like me</i>
<i>Life is sometimes just hard to foresee </i> ♪

398
00:19:35.333 --> 00:19:41.500
<i>♪ Holding my breath</i>
<i>I'll step through concrete mountains </i> ♪

399
00:19:41.583 --> 00:19:47.750
<i>♪ I'll overcome it all</i>
<i>And wipe the dust off my face </i> ♪

400
00:19:49.708 --> 00:19:51.458
[stops playing, sighs]

401
00:19:51.542 --> 00:19:55.167
So, it's true.
It really is your song, isn't it?

402
00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:56.083
Uh…

403
00:19:56.167 --> 00:19:59.458
Are you a solo artist? Or is there a band?
Do you perform live on stage as well?

404
00:19:59.542 --> 00:20:02.458
- That's a lot of questions.
- Well, I've been so curious!

405
00:20:02.542 --> 00:20:06.458
I looked, but I couldn't find anything.
No albums, no social media at all.

406
00:20:06.542 --> 00:20:09.167
God, I love that song. I can't believe it.

407
00:20:09.250 --> 00:20:11.542
[gasps] I'm honored!

408
00:20:12.125 --> 00:20:15.917
- [groans] I said, "I'm honored."
- [guitar music playing]

409
00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:18.000
[Nan-young groans]

410
00:20:29.833 --> 00:20:31.750
[beeping]

411
00:20:32.458 --> 00:20:33.792
SPACE EXPLORATION

412
00:20:40.125 --> 00:20:42.125
DR. JOO'S DREAM TO BLOOM FLOWERS ON MARS

413
00:20:42.208 --> 00:20:45.125
MARS EXPLORATION INTERVIEW
AIRS AT THIS TIME TOMORROW

414
00:20:52.083 --> 00:20:54.083
[music fades]

415
00:20:55.292 --> 00:20:57.292
["Love the Way" playing]

416
00:20:59.958 --> 00:21:01.458
[man] Let's have a look.

417
00:21:01.542 --> 00:21:03.833
Potassium and phosphoric acid levels are…

418
00:21:04.667 --> 00:21:07.375
Why, they're… just far too high.

419
00:21:07.875 --> 00:21:11.917
Just what was everyone doing that
they let it get this bad this quickly?

420
00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:13.000
Huh?

421
00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:15.375
Let's see here.

422
00:21:17.542 --> 00:21:21.458
[man singing along to song]
♪ <i>I love your way </i> ♪

423
00:21:23.667 --> 00:21:26.542
♪ <i>Hold me before the dark </i> ♪

424
00:21:27.667 --> 00:21:31.625
Hmm. And where did all the sprouts
from the germination room go?

425
00:21:33.792 --> 00:21:34.875
Huh…

426
00:21:36.500 --> 00:21:38.500
Hey, Dad. I'm here.

427
00:21:39.292 --> 00:21:42.333
- Hmm. Hmm.
- [song continues playing]

428
00:21:43.792 --> 00:21:44.792
[sighs]

429
00:21:46.292 --> 00:21:48.292
Hmm.

430
00:21:48.375 --> 00:21:49.750
- [Nan-young sighs]
- [beeping]

431
00:21:49.833 --> 00:21:51.833
<i>♪ I love your way… ♪</i>

432
00:21:52.750 --> 00:21:54.250
[beeping continues]

433
00:21:57.667 --> 00:21:59.958
[beeping continues]

434
00:22:00.042 --> 00:22:03.417
[reporter] <i>Thanks to a social media post</i>
<i>by the Korean Space Agency,</i>

435
00:22:03.500 --> 00:22:06.250
<i>the public has finally caught a glimpse
of the life detection device</i>

436
00:22:06.333 --> 00:22:07.458
<i>you've been developing.</i>

437
00:22:07.542 --> 00:22:11.125
<i>What are the chances it will encounter
real Martians during the expedition?</i>

438
00:22:11.208 --> 00:22:12.083
[Nan-young exhales]

439
00:22:12.167 --> 00:22:15.292
The life-forms we are hoping to find
are generally microorganisms,

440
00:22:15.375 --> 00:22:18.250
or more specifically, we are looking for
traces of organic matter

441
00:22:18.333 --> 00:22:20.708
that is emitted by microorganisms
via respiration.

442
00:22:20.792 --> 00:22:23.000
Wow! That sounds fascinating, Dr. Joo.

443
00:22:23.583 --> 00:22:25.875
So you're saying
that the Martians we might meet

444
00:22:25.958 --> 00:22:27.542
will be microorganisms, right?

445
00:22:28.125 --> 00:22:29.500
[Nan-young and others laugh]

446
00:22:29.583 --> 00:22:30.667
Yes, we might just.

447
00:22:30.750 --> 00:22:33.417
[reporter] <i>I admit, this next question</i>
<i>might be a bit sensitive.</i>

448
00:22:33.500 --> 00:22:35.750
<i>Your mother was the late Son Ji-young,</i>

449
00:22:35.833 --> 00:22:39.542
<i>one of the astronauts who passed away
during a previous expedition to Mars.</i>

450
00:22:39.625 --> 00:22:43.042
<i>I'm sure many of our viewers
also remember her as well.</i>

451
00:22:43.125 --> 00:22:46.375
<i>How and why did you decide to pursue
being not just an astronaut</i>

452
00:22:46.458 --> 00:22:47.958
<i>but a Martian explorer?</i>

453
00:22:48.042 --> 00:22:51.750
- Oh, well, uh… uh… to be honest…
- [sound distortion]

454
00:22:51.833 --> 00:22:54.375
I… I don't really remember much about her.

455
00:22:54.458 --> 00:22:55.875
[poignant music playing]

456
00:22:55.958 --> 00:22:57.000
Uh…

457
00:22:57.625 --> 00:22:59.000
MOM'S ON MARS
MOM ISN'T ON MARS

458
00:23:04.750 --> 00:23:07.125
[high-pitched ringing]

459
00:23:09.167 --> 00:23:11.250
[music intensifies, recedes]

460
00:23:11.333 --> 00:23:12.875
- [panelist] Dr. Joo?
- [gasps]

461
00:23:13.625 --> 00:23:15.875
Yes. [Exhales] Sorry about that.

462
00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:19.875
[reporter] <i>I admit, this next question</i>
<i>might be a bit sensitive.</i>

463
00:23:19.958 --> 00:23:21.875
<i>Your mother was the late Son Ji-young,</i>

464
00:23:21.958 --> 00:23:25.875
<i>one of the astronauts who passed away
during a previous expedition to Mars.</i>

465
00:23:25.958 --> 00:23:28.792
<i>I'm sure many of our viewers
also remember her as well.</i>

466
00:23:28.875 --> 00:23:31.875
<i>How and why did you decide to pursue
being not just an astronaut</i>

467
00:23:31.958 --> 00:23:33.583
<i>but a Martian explorer?</i>

468
00:23:33.667 --> 00:23:35.667
[music continues]

469
00:23:38.833 --> 00:23:39.833
[sighs]

470
00:23:42.500 --> 00:23:43.625
[watch dings]

471
00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:48.250
RECORD PLAYER: IT'S RAINING…

472
00:23:48.333 --> 00:23:49.917
LET'S GET SOME OF THIS

473
00:23:50.000 --> 00:23:52.500
- [Jay groans] I'm stuffed.
- [Nan-young] Tell me about it.

474
00:23:52.583 --> 00:23:55.625
Nothing like a tasty meal to cheer you up
when you're feeling down.

475
00:23:56.333 --> 00:23:57.542
[Jay] Hmm.

476
00:23:58.083 --> 00:24:00.708
Yeah, uh, when you're feeling down,

477
00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:04.667
you could, uh…
you could always talk to me about it.

478
00:24:05.167 --> 00:24:07.250
- Hmm?
- Of course you don't have to.

479
00:24:08.958 --> 00:24:10.167
[awkward chuckle]

480
00:24:12.542 --> 00:24:13.542
Hmm.

481
00:24:13.583 --> 00:24:15.708
Well, then, do you mind
if I ask you something?

482
00:24:16.292 --> 00:24:17.292
[Jay] Fire away.

483
00:24:17.833 --> 00:24:21.167
So… how did you get into music?

484
00:24:22.083 --> 00:24:24.083
- Oh. Wow.
- [both chuckle]

485
00:24:24.167 --> 00:24:28.125
It's, uh… hmm…
It's not too exciting, I'm afraid.

486
00:24:28.708 --> 00:24:30.250
- [Nan-young chuckles]
- [Jay] Hmm.

487
00:24:31.042 --> 00:24:32.500
When I was growing up,

488
00:24:32.583 --> 00:24:35.375
I was basically raised
by my grandfather in the countryside.

489
00:24:35.458 --> 00:24:38.333
I had to go with him
to the public bathhouse.

490
00:24:38.417 --> 00:24:41.583
He'd scrub me with this awful brush.
I hated it.

491
00:24:42.292 --> 00:24:43.750
And I let everyone know too.

492
00:24:43.833 --> 00:24:47.583
Whenever he'd take me to the baths,
I'd cry and cry, calling out for my mom.

493
00:24:48.167 --> 00:24:50.250
He taught me to sing
so that I wouldn't cry.

494
00:24:51.333 --> 00:24:54.458
He told me he'd buy me a Coke
if I didn't cry.

495
00:24:54.542 --> 00:24:55.625
Simple enough.

496
00:24:55.708 --> 00:24:57.375
[both laugh]

497
00:24:58.292 --> 00:25:01.333
Aw, sweet little baby Jay.
Must have been cute!

498
00:25:01.417 --> 00:25:02.583
I was cute as a button.

499
00:25:02.667 --> 00:25:04.625
- [laughs]
- Grown-up Jay turned out even better.

500
00:25:04.708 --> 00:25:06.792
- Pretty handsome.
- Okay.

501
00:25:06.875 --> 00:25:08.417
- Uh-oh. You stay here.
- Huh?

502
00:25:08.500 --> 00:25:10.083
- I'll go get us some more.
- Oh.

503
00:25:10.167 --> 00:25:12.407
I'll go too. Don't want this cutie pie
getting kidnapped.

504
00:25:12.458 --> 00:25:14.125
[both laugh]

505
00:25:14.208 --> 00:25:15.708
[Jay] All right, all right.

506
00:25:16.208 --> 00:25:18.292
[chuckles, sighs]

507
00:25:20.417 --> 00:25:22.167
What's grown-up Jay thinking now?

508
00:25:22.250 --> 00:25:23.792
I guess he's probably…

509
00:25:23.875 --> 00:25:25.375
He's probably just waiting.

510
00:25:26.500 --> 00:25:29.875
Waiting for his desire to sing
to come back to him.

511
00:25:30.708 --> 00:25:31.708
Hmm.

512
00:25:33.500 --> 00:25:35.750
[gentle music playing]

513
00:25:37.958 --> 00:25:38.958
[Nan-young] Hmm.

514
00:25:45.375 --> 00:25:46.792
There. Now it's back.

515
00:25:50.333 --> 00:25:51.500
[music fades]

516
00:25:52.083 --> 00:25:54.875
When I was a little girl,
my father would take me stargazing.

517
00:25:54.958 --> 00:25:58.042
I always wondered
what could be out there in space.

518
00:25:58.125 --> 00:26:01.083
And he would just go on and on
about Mars this, Mars that.

519
00:26:01.167 --> 00:26:03.875
[laughs] You could call it brainwashing.

520
00:26:03.958 --> 00:26:06.958
So then we have your father to thank
for your Mars obsession?

521
00:26:07.042 --> 00:26:08.292
[laughs] Sure do.

522
00:26:09.042 --> 00:26:11.542
I guess I wanted to be someone special.

523
00:26:11.625 --> 00:26:14.375
One of the few people on Earth
who get to go to Mars.

524
00:26:15.000 --> 00:26:16.792
- Pretty special.
- Hmm.

525
00:26:19.875 --> 00:26:21.333
- Nan-young.
- Hmm?

526
00:26:22.500 --> 00:26:24.083
You're already special.

527
00:26:24.167 --> 00:26:27.333
Doesn't matter to me
if you're up there or down here.

528
00:26:29.500 --> 00:26:32.042
- I know what you're trying to do.
- [Jay] What?

529
00:26:32.125 --> 00:26:34.042
All those compliments. Hmm.

530
00:26:34.625 --> 00:26:35.875
[Jay laughs]

531
00:26:35.958 --> 00:26:38.875
I should tell you now.
Just so you know, it won't work.

532
00:26:40.292 --> 00:26:43.917
Because one day,
I might just fly off into space.

533
00:26:44.000 --> 00:26:45.250
Maybe, but for now…

534
00:26:46.583 --> 00:26:47.500
Huh?

535
00:26:47.583 --> 00:26:48.792
…you're a backup, right?

536
00:26:49.542 --> 00:26:50.542
[chuckles]

537
00:26:52.250 --> 00:26:53.667
- [Nan-young grunts]
- [Jay] Huh?

538
00:26:53.750 --> 00:26:54.833
Still, we can't.

539
00:26:54.917 --> 00:26:56.958
["Purple Stereo" playing]

540
00:26:57.042 --> 00:27:00.833
[cries out] I can't! No commitments!

541
00:27:00.917 --> 00:27:02.958
Eyes on the prize! Ugh.

542
00:27:03.042 --> 00:27:04.750
[laughs]

543
00:27:05.500 --> 00:27:06.708
What commitment?

544
00:27:06.792 --> 00:27:08.250
- Stay away.
- Huh?

545
00:27:09.250 --> 00:27:11.125
[laughs]

546
00:27:11.208 --> 00:27:13.125
- Let's keep our distance.
- Distance?

547
00:27:14.250 --> 00:27:15.917
- Uh.
- Hmm.

548
00:27:16.000 --> 00:27:16.875
[Nan-young] Mm.

549
00:27:16.958 --> 00:27:18.333
- [Jay laughs]
- Don't!

550
00:27:18.417 --> 00:27:19.583
[both laugh]

551
00:27:22.583 --> 00:27:24.500
[man] Hey! What's all the racket
down there?

552
00:27:24.583 --> 00:27:26.333
What? Do you think you own the place, huh?

553
00:27:26.417 --> 00:27:29.333
- Sorry! Sorry! Sorry!
- Sorry! Sorry!

554
00:27:30.125 --> 00:27:31.958
[both laugh]

555
00:27:32.042 --> 00:27:34.708
<i>♪ Ashes to our love… ♪</i>

556
00:27:34.792 --> 00:27:36.458
[Nan-young] Come on, come on!

557
00:27:36.542 --> 00:27:38.542
[both laugh]

558
00:27:38.625 --> 00:27:41.250
<i>♪ We've always been here ♪</i>

559
00:27:41.333 --> 00:27:43.333
[laughing heartily]

560
00:27:45.292 --> 00:27:48.667
<i>♪ We running on the stereo ♪</i>

561
00:27:50.083 --> 00:27:51.958
- [Jay yells]
- [Nan-young yells, laughs]

562
00:27:52.042 --> 00:27:53.708
<i>♪ Always been here… ♪</i>

563
00:27:53.792 --> 00:27:55.667
[Jay] Oh…

564
00:27:55.750 --> 00:27:58.000
Are you okay? Oh dear.

565
00:27:58.083 --> 00:27:59.500
- [Nan-young laughs]
- Oh boy.

566
00:28:00.208 --> 00:28:02.792
I'm so sorry. Sorry about that.

567
00:28:02.875 --> 00:28:04.500
[both laugh]

568
00:28:04.583 --> 00:28:07.042
<i>♪ Staying still here ♪</i>

569
00:28:07.125 --> 00:28:08.250
Here, let me see.

570
00:28:10.833 --> 00:28:14.417
<i>♪ We whisper under purple glow ♪</i>

571
00:28:14.500 --> 00:28:17.542
[both panting]

572
00:28:20.583 --> 00:28:22.292
It's complicated, Jay.

573
00:28:29.083 --> 00:28:30.083
What is?

574
00:28:31.333 --> 00:28:33.333
[both breathing heavily]

575
00:28:35.292 --> 00:28:36.458
[Nan-young moans]

576
00:28:39.708 --> 00:28:41.708
[elevator whirring]

577
00:28:42.708 --> 00:28:47.583
<i>♪ We've always been here ♪</i>

578
00:28:49.375 --> 00:28:52.500
<i>♪ We running on the stereo ♪</i>

579
00:28:56.083 --> 00:29:00.375
<i>♪ Always been here ♪</i>

580
00:29:02.125 --> 00:29:05.375
<i>♪ We wonder why we found the love ♪</i>

581
00:29:07.833 --> 00:29:09.833
<i>♪ A lot of melodies ♪</i>

582
00:29:09.917 --> 00:29:14.208
<i>♪ I love your fingers
Playing sounds of Billie ♪</i>

583
00:29:14.292 --> 00:29:16.458
<i>♪ Purple romance ♪</i>

584
00:29:18.167 --> 00:29:19.875
<i>♪ The glowing ♪</i>

585
00:29:20.917 --> 00:29:24.375
<i>♪ It's a favorite scene for you and me ♪</i>

586
00:29:24.458 --> 00:29:29.500
<i>♪ We dancing on the stereo
The one last ♪</i>

587
00:29:30.875 --> 00:29:33.042
<i>♪ The one last time ♪</i>

588
00:29:37.292 --> 00:29:42.375
<i>♪ The one last time ♪</i>

589
00:29:43.542 --> 00:29:48.333
<i>♪ We've always been here ♪</i>

590
00:29:50.167 --> 00:29:53.375
<i>♪ We running on the stereo ♪</i>

591
00:29:56.875 --> 00:30:01.042
<i>♪ Always been here ♪</i>

592
00:30:02.167 --> 00:30:03.333
[song ends]

593
00:30:03.417 --> 00:30:06.083
<i>Ah! Do you ever sleep?</i>

594
00:30:06.167 --> 00:30:09.792
Yeah, I feel like I'm so close,
but I just can't work this out!

595
00:30:10.333 --> 00:30:13.958
Layers A and B with a mesh weave,
then B and C on top.

596
00:30:14.042 --> 00:30:17.458
Ugh, that's already too thick. [Groans]

597
00:30:17.542 --> 00:30:21.417
[sighs] I need to finish this,
so someone can take it to Mars.

598
00:30:21.500 --> 00:30:23.292
[yawns]

599
00:30:23.375 --> 00:30:24.708
<i>Just a sec.</i>

600
00:30:24.792 --> 00:30:26.958
<i>- That someone is me, isn't it? Am I wrong?</i>
- [yawns]

601
00:30:27.750 --> 00:30:29.167
<i>- Joo Nan-young.</i>
- Hmm?

602
00:30:29.250 --> 00:30:32.750
<i>If you want me to go, you're gonna have</i>
<i>to tell me to my </i>natjjak.

603
00:30:32.833 --> 00:30:34.208
Practicing Korean?

604
00:30:34.292 --> 00:30:35.892
[Rosa] <i>I'm getting better thanks to you,</i>

605
00:30:35.958 --> 00:30:38.292
<i>but I'll be sure to master it
once I start dating.</i>

606
00:30:38.375 --> 00:30:39.750
- Oh, Rosa.
- [Rosa laughs]

607
00:30:39.833 --> 00:30:41.792
You're gonna miss out on dating on Mars.

608
00:30:41.875 --> 00:30:45.000
<i>Speaking of which, how's it going
for you and that artist guy?</i>

609
00:30:45.083 --> 00:30:46.542
- [watch dings]
- [Rosa] <i>Huh?</i>

610
00:30:46.625 --> 00:30:49.625
<i>Oh, speak of the devil.</i>
<i>This is him, right? It's him! </i>[Laughs]

611
00:30:49.708 --> 00:30:52.500
<i>- Hello? You must be the man…</i>
- Rosa!

612
00:30:52.583 --> 00:30:54.904
<i>…that Nan-young's been mooning over.
She's totally in love.</i>

613
00:30:54.958 --> 00:30:56.625
- Cut it out, Rosa!
- [Rosa laughs]

614
00:30:56.708 --> 00:30:59.000
He… hello? Hey, Jay.

615
00:30:59.500 --> 00:31:00.792
Outside? Now?

616
00:31:00.875 --> 00:31:01.750
<i>Huh?</i>

617
00:31:01.833 --> 00:31:03.833
[drone whirring]

618
00:31:04.875 --> 00:31:08.458
LET'S CELEBRATE! HAPPY BIRTHDAY, MARS GEEK

619
00:31:11.667 --> 00:31:12.833
[chuckles]

620
00:31:13.417 --> 00:31:15.417
[laughs heartily]

621
00:31:16.750 --> 00:31:18.750
[both laugh]

622
00:31:20.458 --> 00:31:22.458
[creaking]

623
00:31:24.667 --> 00:31:25.667
Hmm.

624
00:31:26.833 --> 00:31:28.792
That should work.

625
00:31:29.917 --> 00:31:33.292
[Nan-young] I told you, didn't I?
He's a certified Mars fanatic.

626
00:31:33.375 --> 00:31:34.958
He's got quite the setup.

627
00:31:35.042 --> 00:31:37.875
Like an undercover Earth warrior spy.

628
00:31:37.958 --> 00:31:39.292
[Nan-young chuckles]

629
00:31:39.375 --> 00:31:41.667
He's transmitting to space right now.

630
00:31:41.750 --> 00:31:44.875
He thinks someone on Mars
wants to wish me a very happy birthday.

631
00:31:46.208 --> 00:31:48.875
[Jay] So then, he's sending a message
to your mom, huh?

632
00:31:49.917 --> 00:31:52.667
- Uh, how did you know?
- Sorry.

633
00:31:53.458 --> 00:31:55.083
When your girlfriend's famous,

634
00:31:55.167 --> 00:31:57.208
a web search brings up
more than her birthday.

635
00:31:58.000 --> 00:31:59.000
[sighs]

636
00:31:59.583 --> 00:32:01.792
Now you know
that he's trying to reach my mother.

637
00:32:01.875 --> 00:32:04.250
And has been doing so
for the last 20 years.

638
00:32:04.333 --> 00:32:06.333
I don't think he believes she's gone.

639
00:32:07.000 --> 00:32:08.083
[Jay sighs]

640
00:32:08.167 --> 00:32:11.750
It's a birthday tradition to come here
and send a message off to Mars.

641
00:32:11.833 --> 00:32:14.667
Well, then, from here on out,
you can count me in too.

642
00:32:15.208 --> 00:32:17.458
[father] Okay, the transmission
has been engaged.

643
00:32:17.542 --> 00:32:19.792
I know it looks small,
but it's really rather effective.

644
00:32:19.875 --> 00:32:21.417
Do you mind if I take a look with you?

645
00:32:21.500 --> 00:32:23.708
Not at all. Here, you take the driver...

646
00:32:23.792 --> 00:32:25.458
[exclaims]

647
00:32:25.542 --> 00:32:27.500
[both exclaiming]

648
00:32:29.875 --> 00:32:30.875
[both apologizing]

649
00:32:30.917 --> 00:32:33.333
Don't think you can call yourself
a repairman.

650
00:32:33.417 --> 00:32:35.167
[laughs] You're more like
a destruction man.

651
00:32:35.750 --> 00:32:39.042
[father] This isn't small at all.
This side is completely destroyed.

652
00:32:39.625 --> 00:32:43.750
[Jay] Is this little signal really enough?
Can it make it all the way to Mars?

653
00:32:44.250 --> 00:32:45.833
Radio waves can go anywhere,

654
00:32:45.917 --> 00:32:48.083
but someone has to be there
to receive them.

655
00:32:48.167 --> 00:32:50.667
Hmm… Once the antenna
at the base is completed,

656
00:32:50.750 --> 00:32:52.542
we'll be able to make live calls.

657
00:32:52.625 --> 00:32:54.292
Well, with a 20-minute delay.

658
00:32:55.750 --> 00:32:57.583
- [Jay] Listen, Nan-young.
- Hmm?

659
00:32:57.667 --> 00:33:00.125
If you do end up being chosen
to go to Mars,

660
00:33:00.208 --> 00:33:01.583
how will I contact you?

661
00:33:02.208 --> 00:33:04.792
By… walkie-talkie?

662
00:33:04.875 --> 00:33:05.958
[laughs] Jay!

663
00:33:06.042 --> 00:33:08.750
- [both laugh]
- [Nan-young sighs]

664
00:33:10.500 --> 00:33:11.500
Do you think…

665
00:33:13.000 --> 00:33:15.583
That I'll get to go to space? To Mars?

666
00:33:16.417 --> 00:33:17.417
We could go right now.

667
00:33:17.875 --> 00:33:19.417
- [Nan-young] Hmm?
- Together.

668
00:33:20.458 --> 00:33:21.958
- Huh.
- [piano music playing]

669
00:33:22.042 --> 00:33:23.375
[Nan-young] That one. Yeah, look.

670
00:33:23.458 --> 00:33:25.542
- [Jay] This one?
- It's so cute.

671
00:33:25.625 --> 00:33:28.333
Ooh, here it comes.
It's dropping now! Wow!

672
00:33:28.417 --> 00:33:30.458
- [Jay] Looks so tasty!
- [Nan-young] Sure does!

673
00:33:30.542 --> 00:33:32.500
[Jay] I've never been to an observatory.

674
00:33:32.583 --> 00:33:34.583
- I can't remember the last time. Whoa!
- Whoa!

675
00:33:36.333 --> 00:33:39.083
- What's that constellation?
- I'm not sure.

676
00:33:40.792 --> 00:33:42.167
[Nan-young chuckles]

677
00:33:43.000 --> 00:33:44.083
[Jay gasps]

678
00:33:47.208 --> 00:33:49.042
Jay, there it is. That's Mars.

679
00:33:49.625 --> 00:33:51.542
- Where? Which one?
- Right there.

680
00:33:51.625 --> 00:33:54.625
Oh! Doesn't seem that far at all, huh?

681
00:33:54.708 --> 00:33:57.059
[Nan-young] I told you.
Spatially speaking, it's very close.

682
00:33:57.083 --> 00:33:59.292
[Jay] But it takes six months
to get there.

683
00:33:59.375 --> 00:34:01.750
[Nan-young] Ah, six months
is nothing in space.

684
00:34:03.292 --> 00:34:07.292
[young Nan-young] Wow.
It doesn't look that far.

685
00:34:08.958 --> 00:34:12.833
It's so close, right?
You'll be back home soon.

686
00:34:13.417 --> 00:34:14.833
- [chuckles]
- [sighs]

687
00:34:15.542 --> 00:34:17.958
Isn't that right, Mom? [Laughs]

688
00:34:21.125 --> 00:34:22.875
[both cry out]

689
00:34:38.250 --> 00:34:40.292
Why did you lie to me, Mommy?

690
00:34:40.375 --> 00:34:41.833
<i>You lied to me!</i>

691
00:34:41.917 --> 00:34:43.958
<i>You said that you'd be back soon.</i>

692
00:34:44.458 --> 00:34:45.875
<i>Why did you lie to me?</i>

693
00:34:45.958 --> 00:34:47.000
[yelling]

694
00:34:47.083 --> 00:34:49.292
[young Nan-young] <i>I miss my mommy.</i>

695
00:34:49.375 --> 00:34:50.708
[Nan-young crying out]

696
00:34:50.792 --> 00:34:52.500
[young Nan-young] <i>Get her back for me!</i>

697
00:34:54.500 --> 00:34:55.500
<i>I miss her.</i>

698
00:34:56.417 --> 00:34:57.583
Don't go!

699
00:34:59.083 --> 00:35:00.375
<i>I love you too, Mommy.</i>

700
00:35:02.625 --> 00:35:04.667
- [echoing] <i>Liar.</i>
- [gasps]

701
00:35:08.250 --> 00:35:10.750
Nan-young,
do you want rice or toast with...

702
00:35:11.375 --> 00:35:13.083
Oh. What's the matter?

703
00:35:13.583 --> 00:35:14.958
Why are you crying?

704
00:35:15.458 --> 00:35:17.833
- Oh.
- [sobbing] It's nothing.

705
00:35:19.625 --> 00:35:21.000
It's just a dream.

706
00:35:21.875 --> 00:35:23.458
Nightmares, they say…

707
00:35:24.875 --> 00:35:27.417
Are vanquished by the morning sunshine.

708
00:35:27.500 --> 00:35:28.625
Huh? Oh.

709
00:35:32.042 --> 00:35:33.833
Is this a greenhouse?

710
00:35:34.333 --> 00:35:36.083
I didn't know
that you were into gardening.

711
00:35:36.167 --> 00:35:38.250
Uh, not earth gardening anyway.

712
00:35:38.917 --> 00:35:41.958
- [beeps]
- [Jay] Oh. Whoa. Ooh.

713
00:35:42.042 --> 00:35:43.417
Who's this guy?

714
00:35:43.500 --> 00:35:47.708
It's a detector that can find even
the tiniest traces of micro organic life.

715
00:35:48.417 --> 00:35:51.375
The culmination of my hard work.
That's him.

716
00:35:51.458 --> 00:35:52.625
- Right?
- [Jay laughs]

717
00:35:53.792 --> 00:35:57.792
Wow. I have no idea what
you're talking about, but it's incredible.

718
00:35:57.875 --> 00:35:59.625
- Hey, it is!
- [Jay laughs]

719
00:36:02.000 --> 00:36:03.708
Of course it is. You made it.

720
00:36:03.792 --> 00:36:04.917
[detector trills]

721
00:36:05.000 --> 00:36:06.167
- Amur Adonis.
- Whoa.

722
00:36:06.250 --> 00:36:08.833
They're unique
because they bloom in the snow.

723
00:36:08.917 --> 00:36:11.792
When they bloom,
they give off a small amount of heat.

724
00:36:12.458 --> 00:36:15.667
These samples have been engineered
to maximize self-heating.

725
00:36:15.750 --> 00:36:19.042
And with them, we're going to make
a flower garden on Mars.

726
00:36:19.542 --> 00:36:23.250
These will be like the protective parents.
Here you go.

727
00:36:23.333 --> 00:36:24.208
[detector beeps]

728
00:36:24.292 --> 00:36:25.833
They look pretty safe in there.

729
00:36:25.917 --> 00:36:28.250
What, with a fancy beam projector
and armored greenhouse.

730
00:36:28.333 --> 00:36:29.458
[Nan-young laughs]

731
00:36:31.208 --> 00:36:33.625
- You weren't listening at all, were you?
- [Jay laughs]

732
00:36:33.708 --> 00:36:37.125
Dr. Joo, I do need to buckle down
and study more.

733
00:36:37.208 --> 00:36:40.500
Today's practical experiment will involve
the self-heating capabilities of Jay,

734
00:36:40.583 --> 00:36:42.750
engineered to protect Joo Nan-young.

735
00:36:42.833 --> 00:36:44.000
Get away from me!

736
00:36:44.083 --> 00:36:46.083
[both laugh]

737
00:36:51.208 --> 00:36:53.500
[Nan-young] I guess I must have been
about five or so.

738
00:36:53.583 --> 00:36:56.250
I made an astronaut like this one
with art supplies.

739
00:36:57.042 --> 00:36:58.917
Seems like
you've been thinking about space

740
00:36:59.000 --> 00:37:01.042
since before you started walking.

741
00:37:01.125 --> 00:37:05.208
Oh, I just realized that little astronaut
made it to space before I did.

742
00:37:05.292 --> 00:37:06.583
- Hmm.
- How is that?

743
00:37:07.250 --> 00:37:08.750
My mom took him.

744
00:37:08.833 --> 00:37:12.458
Since I obviously couldn't go along,
she took him in my place.

745
00:37:13.000 --> 00:37:14.833
I remember how I collected candy wrappers

746
00:37:14.917 --> 00:37:18.250
for what seemed like months
so that I could make his suit shiny.

747
00:37:18.333 --> 00:37:19.625
That's amazing, you know?

748
00:37:19.708 --> 00:37:21.958
That you can remember those details
from your childhood.

749
00:37:23.458 --> 00:37:24.833
[Nan-young] It's weird, right?

750
00:37:25.917 --> 00:37:28.917
I remember all that,
but sometimes I forget how she looked.

751
00:37:31.250 --> 00:37:32.583
Candy wrappers…

752
00:37:33.750 --> 00:37:35.042
<i>As C and D.</i>

753
00:37:35.833 --> 00:37:39.208
Scotch tape for B.

754
00:37:39.792 --> 00:37:42.000
- Popsicle stick as A.
- [Jay] Hmm.

755
00:37:43.375 --> 00:37:44.417
[Nan-young gasps]

756
00:37:44.500 --> 00:37:45.917
A on its own!

757
00:37:46.000 --> 00:37:48.125
If A is an independent material,
it should work!

758
00:37:48.208 --> 00:37:49.667
What… what are you talking... Ah!

759
00:37:49.750 --> 00:37:52.125
Whoa. What's going on?

760
00:37:52.792 --> 00:37:54.458
If A is laid out independently,

761
00:37:54.958 --> 00:37:57.500
then B can be laid between C and D.

762
00:37:59.750 --> 00:38:01.000
[beeping]

763
00:38:02.292 --> 00:38:03.292
[Nan-young gasps]

764
00:38:04.167 --> 00:38:05.167
Eureka!

765
00:38:05.583 --> 00:38:06.417
[detector] <i>Scanning.</i>

766
00:38:06.500 --> 00:38:09.292
There are a few functions
that need to be tweaked and fine-tuned.

767
00:38:10.375 --> 00:38:11.917
- [chuckles]
<i>- Scanning target.</i>

768
00:38:12.000 --> 00:38:15.333
But even in its current state,
the sensitivity and speed are perfect.

769
00:38:15.417 --> 00:38:16.667
Good work.

770
00:38:16.750 --> 00:38:19.125
[woman] Nicely done, Dr. Joo. Great work!

771
00:38:19.208 --> 00:38:21.875
[deputy director] Microorganisms.
In the clean room!

772
00:38:21.958 --> 00:38:23.875
Who was on sterilization duty?

773
00:38:23.958 --> 00:38:25.083
[chuckles]

774
00:38:25.958 --> 00:38:27.958
[jazzy music playing]

775
00:38:29.417 --> 00:38:31.917
[Nan-young] I have earned
another one of these.

776
00:38:32.542 --> 00:38:33.625
And you?

777
00:38:33.708 --> 00:38:35.000
Just another Coke?

778
00:38:35.500 --> 00:38:38.958
I just made a groundbreaking discovery!
Dinner is my treat.

779
00:38:39.042 --> 00:38:40.750
Mmm. Coke is fine.

780
00:38:42.625 --> 00:38:44.625
[band tuning instruments]

781
00:38:46.583 --> 00:38:48.000
They're gonna play a show.

782
00:38:49.417 --> 00:38:51.417
[band starts to play]

783
00:38:54.667 --> 00:38:57.417
<i>♪ A sea of stars ♪</i>

784
00:38:58.125 --> 00:39:02.833
<i>♪ Where everything sparkles
The way they do ♪</i>

785
00:39:04.167 --> 00:39:07.750
<i>♪ Are you here to tell you mattered… ♪</i>

786
00:39:07.833 --> 00:39:08.833
Wow.

787
00:39:09.583 --> 00:39:10.833
It's nice.

788
00:39:12.292 --> 00:39:13.292
[chuckles softly]

789
00:39:14.708 --> 00:39:16.708
[people chattering]

790
00:39:18.542 --> 00:39:21.917
No. Yeah, I saw them last week too,
and they were amazing. So good.

791
00:39:24.125 --> 00:39:25.333
Jay.

792
00:39:31.500 --> 00:39:32.500
Hey.

793
00:39:35.208 --> 00:39:37.167
You're not answering my messages.

794
00:39:38.208 --> 00:39:40.083
There isn't anything for us to talk about.

795
00:39:40.167 --> 00:39:42.792
[woman] Whatever.
Just keep running away, Jay.

796
00:39:42.875 --> 00:39:44.375
[Jay exhales angrily]

797
00:39:44.458 --> 00:39:48.000
You know, a lot of people out there
still like your music.

798
00:39:48.083 --> 00:39:49.125
My music?

799
00:39:49.792 --> 00:39:51.667
Yes, that's my music.

800
00:39:51.750 --> 00:39:53.750
- And you're using it for yourself.
- Our next show.

801
00:39:53.833 --> 00:39:56.042
- Jay. Oh.
- The Panda Sound team is coming.

802
00:39:56.125 --> 00:39:58.083
You know, that label you love so much?

803
00:39:58.792 --> 00:40:02.250
- Uh. I'm sorry. Let's go.
- [Nan-young] Uh, okay.

804
00:40:02.333 --> 00:40:05.000
[woman] Saturday. Rolling Burn.
We go on at eight.

805
00:40:05.083 --> 00:40:06.083
You should come too.

806
00:40:06.167 --> 00:40:08.958
Jay's pretty impressive
when he plays live.

807
00:40:11.875 --> 00:40:14.333
Hmm. She's just an old band mate.

808
00:40:14.833 --> 00:40:16.625
But we're not friends anymore.

809
00:40:17.458 --> 00:40:19.250
Sorry about that.

810
00:40:19.333 --> 00:40:20.833
[sighs] It's all right.

811
00:40:22.708 --> 00:40:24.375
But I would like to see it.

812
00:40:24.875 --> 00:40:26.500
You on stage.

813
00:40:27.000 --> 00:40:29.292
I tried looking it up,
but there's nothing.

814
00:40:29.375 --> 00:40:31.667
Hmm. Do you have any videos of it?

815
00:40:32.542 --> 00:40:33.583
Hmm?

816
00:40:34.417 --> 00:40:35.708
- Hmm.
- [beep]

817
00:40:44.542 --> 00:40:46.583
[Jay] Di-a! Di-a! Look over here. Di-a.

818
00:40:46.667 --> 00:40:49.792
Cut it out!
Stop recording, or I'll kill you!

819
00:40:49.875 --> 00:40:51.875
[crowd cheering]

820
00:40:52.458 --> 00:40:54.208
[guitar riff plays]

821
00:40:54.292 --> 00:40:56.292
[tense music playing]

822
00:40:56.375 --> 00:40:58.375
[guitar riff continues]

823
00:41:02.125 --> 00:41:03.125
[music fades]

824
00:41:04.125 --> 00:41:07.083
[Di-a] <i>What's wrong? You don't like it?</i>

825
00:41:07.667 --> 00:41:09.792
I think it started to fall a little flat.

826
00:41:10.375 --> 00:41:12.958
So I tweaked it a bit.
Made it better for live performance.

827
00:41:13.042 --> 00:41:14.292
[Jay chuckles angrily]

828
00:41:15.083 --> 00:41:16.958
You haven't changed at all, have you?

829
00:41:17.667 --> 00:41:20.958
I… it barely sounds like my song,
and the chorus lyrics…

830
00:41:21.708 --> 00:41:22.708
[scoffs]

831
00:41:22.750 --> 00:41:25.458
Since you can't sing it,
it never would have seen the light of day.

832
00:41:25.542 --> 00:41:28.125
You should be happy
someone wants to sing it at all.

833
00:41:28.208 --> 00:41:31.417
Just forget it. I don't know why
I should expect anything else.

834
00:41:32.250 --> 00:41:33.958
Good luck without a guitarist.

835
00:41:34.042 --> 00:41:36.417
The tone in your voice
made me think you might've changed.

836
00:41:36.500 --> 00:41:38.000
[Di-a] If you leave now, well,

837
00:41:38.083 --> 00:41:40.667
then whatever this is
will be your life forever.

838
00:41:41.250 --> 00:41:43.417
You won't get another chance, Jay.

839
00:41:44.083 --> 00:41:46.000
One last shot
to make up for all your mistakes.

840
00:41:46.083 --> 00:41:48.583
- [crowd cheering]
- [muffled music playing]

841
00:41:48.667 --> 00:41:51.042
- [man] Hold up. Are you back?
- [Jay] Huh?

842
00:41:51.125 --> 00:41:53.542
Come on, join us. Let's put on a show!

843
00:41:54.667 --> 00:41:56.083
[crowd cheering]

844
00:41:56.167 --> 00:41:58.167
[muffled music playing in background]

845
00:41:59.792 --> 00:42:01.125
[tapping microphone]

846
00:42:01.208 --> 00:42:02.750
- [Di-a sighs]
- [crowd cheers]

847
00:42:03.333 --> 00:42:04.917
[Di-a] We're on the last song already?

848
00:42:05.000 --> 00:42:06.375
[man] Over here, over here!

849
00:42:06.458 --> 00:42:08.833
We've got a surprise band member
joining us.

850
00:42:08.917 --> 00:42:11.458
- I think you all remember him, don't you?
- [crowd yelling] Yeah!

851
00:42:12.042 --> 00:42:14.417
On guitar, Jay!

852
00:42:15.125 --> 00:42:16.125
[clapping]

853
00:42:17.333 --> 00:42:18.792
- [Di-a laughs]
- [crowd] Jay!

854
00:42:18.875 --> 00:42:20.500
[Di-a] And on that note…

855
00:42:21.208 --> 00:42:24.458
We've got a new song for you all tonight,
something special from The Moles.

856
00:42:25.417 --> 00:42:27.208
Written by him.

857
00:42:28.083 --> 00:42:29.000
"Stay."

858
00:42:29.083 --> 00:42:30.792
[crowd cheering]

859
00:42:30.875 --> 00:42:32.875
[mellow guitar music playing]

860
00:42:38.167 --> 00:42:39.167
[clears throat]

861
00:42:42.792 --> 00:42:45.042
[Jay] Hyung, you should come in
right here.

862
00:42:45.125 --> 00:42:46.125
Mmm.

863
00:42:47.833 --> 00:42:49.708
I'll send this version to the label.

864
00:42:49.792 --> 00:42:50.792
Um… uh…

865
00:42:53.958 --> 00:42:56.667
You went and changed everything around,
and now it's a mess.

866
00:42:56.750 --> 00:42:58.958
- Wait!
- How do you expect me to feel?

867
00:42:59.042 --> 00:43:00.750
The show's starting.
Get on stage now, Jay!

868
00:43:00.833 --> 00:43:02.708
[Jay] I can't! I can't do it anymore!

869
00:43:03.292 --> 00:43:06.167
[Di-a] <i>Nobody cares</i>
<i>about your stupid story.</i>

870
00:43:06.667 --> 00:43:07.667
GARBAGE
JUST A DIARY

871
00:43:08.500 --> 00:43:10.625
[Jay gasping]

872
00:43:12.292 --> 00:43:14.667
[Di-a vocalizing]

873
00:43:16.083 --> 00:43:18.625
<i>♪ Somewhere higher than the clouds ♪</i>

874
00:43:18.708 --> 00:43:20.667
<i>♪ We're dancing with the lights ♪</i>

875
00:43:20.750 --> 00:43:23.083
<i>♪ Baby, don't let go ♪</i>

876
00:43:23.167 --> 00:43:26.458
<i>♪ Stay with me ♪</i>

877
00:43:26.542 --> 00:43:29.750
<i>♪ Like the fairy tales we used to… ♪</i>

878
00:43:29.833 --> 00:43:30.750
[gasps]

879
00:43:30.833 --> 00:43:32.917
He's amazing! Jay!

880
00:43:33.000 --> 00:43:37.292
[laughing joyfully]

881
00:43:39.583 --> 00:43:40.583
Huh?

882
00:43:45.250 --> 00:43:47.667
[Nan-young] Jay,
you really won't sing anymore?

883
00:43:47.750 --> 00:43:48.625
[Jay] Hmm.

884
00:43:48.708 --> 00:43:52.792
I don't know. Even if I rejoin,
Di-a is the singer of the band.

885
00:43:53.917 --> 00:43:56.417
And to be fair,
I don't know if I want to rejoin.

886
00:43:57.042 --> 00:43:58.792
Really? Hmm.

887
00:43:59.500 --> 00:44:01.292
I know I'm not a musician,

888
00:44:01.958 --> 00:44:03.708
but that song, you know.

889
00:44:03.792 --> 00:44:06.583
Your song, I like Jay's version more.

890
00:44:07.708 --> 00:44:10.083
And of course
your performance tonight was impressive.

891
00:44:10.167 --> 00:44:12.042
I just hope there comes a day

892
00:44:12.125 --> 00:44:15.208
when everyone else in the world
can hear your beautiful voice,

893
00:44:15.292 --> 00:44:16.417
and it's not just me.

894
00:44:17.500 --> 00:44:19.292
You don't like private concerts?

895
00:44:19.375 --> 00:44:21.458
Not when I have
such an amazing man to show off.

896
00:44:21.542 --> 00:44:23.625
- [watch dings]
- [Jay chuckles]

897
00:44:23.708 --> 00:44:24.708
Uh.

898
00:44:37.083 --> 00:44:38.250
[gasps]

899
00:44:38.333 --> 00:44:39.583
I made it!

900
00:44:40.083 --> 00:44:42.000
- [Jay] Huh?
- [Nan-young squeals]

901
00:44:43.292 --> 00:44:46.208
- [Jay] What is it? What's going on, huh?
- [Nan-young] It's a secret.

902
00:44:46.292 --> 00:44:48.708
Just celebrate with me, okay?

903
00:44:50.125 --> 00:44:51.458
[Jay chuckles]

904
00:44:53.125 --> 00:44:55.005
[Jay's boss] First you said
you'd never sell it.

905
00:44:55.042 --> 00:44:57.333
Now you're harvesting the thing for parts?

906
00:44:57.417 --> 00:44:59.500
Looks like you've got
something to live for.

907
00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:03.208
Yep. Life's as sweet as it can be.
[chuckles]

908
00:45:03.292 --> 00:45:04.792
Well, all right then.

909
00:45:04.875 --> 00:45:06.875
[siren wailing in the distance]

910
00:45:08.417 --> 00:45:11.625
<i>It hasn't officially been announced yet,
but the team found something</i>

911
00:45:11.708 --> 00:45:15.750
<i>near the lava zone.
A collision crater by sector 6F.</i>

912
00:45:16.292 --> 00:45:17.417
<i>There is a possibility</i>

913
00:45:17.500 --> 00:45:20.958
<i>that the collision crater
contains organic material.</i>

914
00:45:21.042 --> 00:45:24.458
<i>So, if you bring
the life-form detection system,</i>

915
00:45:24.542 --> 00:45:27.000
<i>there'll be a lot work for you
on the mission.</i>

916
00:45:27.083 --> 00:45:30.083
<i>It would be a shame to miss the chance
to discover this amount of data</i>

917
00:45:30.167 --> 00:45:31.625
<i>while we're on Mars.</i>

918
00:45:31.708 --> 00:45:34.750
Thank you.
I'll sleep well tonight, Captain.

919
00:45:35.500 --> 00:45:37.083
<i>It's a bit of a tight schedule,</i>

920
00:45:37.167 --> 00:45:40.542
<i>but send out your last words video
by 0600.</i>

921
00:45:40.625 --> 00:45:43.042
<i>Wrap things up ASAP and return.</i>

922
00:45:43.750 --> 00:45:45.917
<i>- Can you do that?</i>
- Yes, sir.

923
00:45:46.000 --> 00:45:47.000
JAY

924
00:45:47.083 --> 00:45:48.375
[dance music playing]

925
00:45:48.458 --> 00:45:51.083
- Make a wish!
- [Nan-young laughs]

926
00:45:52.708 --> 00:45:55.509
Hey, Chief. The official announcement
doesn't air till tomorrow, right?

927
00:45:55.583 --> 00:45:56.958
That's right. 8 p.m.

928
00:45:57.042 --> 00:45:58.417
No blabbing before then.

929
00:45:58.500 --> 00:46:01.125
[everyone exclaiming and laughing]

930
00:46:01.208 --> 00:46:03.125
Chief, doesn't the announcement
air tonight?

931
00:46:03.208 --> 00:46:05.958
Huh? Dr. Joo! It's on tonight!

932
00:46:06.042 --> 00:46:08.042
- [laughing]
- In two years, I'll be patient.

933
00:46:08.125 --> 00:46:10.000
[Nan-young] All right then.
Before I go, okay?

934
00:46:10.083 --> 00:46:12.542
- [researcher] I'm so happy for you!
- [Nan-young] Cheers!

935
00:46:12.625 --> 00:46:13.750
[door opens]

936
00:46:15.417 --> 00:46:16.708
[lights chime]

937
00:46:18.583 --> 00:46:19.583
Hmm.

938
00:46:20.292 --> 00:46:22.375
- [mellow music playing]
- Hmm.

939
00:46:22.458 --> 00:46:25.417
Oh, Nan-young.
I can see you've been pretty busy.

940
00:46:27.458 --> 00:46:28.583
[grunts]

941
00:46:46.125 --> 00:46:48.125
[humming]

942
00:46:49.167 --> 00:46:50.333
[chuckles]

943
00:46:55.167 --> 00:46:56.208
Where's her vinyl?

944
00:47:00.292 --> 00:47:04.333
Frank Sinatra and Chet Baker?

945
00:47:04.958 --> 00:47:05.958
Huh.

946
00:47:08.042 --> 00:47:09.042
Oh.

947
00:47:10.667 --> 00:47:12.917
Alice Mae King's hit, "Love the Way."

948
00:47:14.542 --> 00:47:16.792
Her mom had a taste for the classics.

949
00:47:16.875 --> 00:47:17.875
Oh!

950
00:47:19.500 --> 00:47:20.792
Hmm. [Sighs]

951
00:47:22.750 --> 00:47:24.292
Oh… a QR code?

952
00:47:25.125 --> 00:47:26.833
Hmm.

953
00:47:27.917 --> 00:47:29.542
[beeps]

954
00:47:29.625 --> 00:47:32.583
[Ji-young] <i>Day 49 on Mars, 9:47 p.m.</i>

955
00:47:33.458 --> 00:47:36.500
<i>The winds calmed down today,
so it was rather mild.</i>

956
00:47:37.625 --> 00:47:40.500
<i>The weather has been
really agreeable lately, so I feel great.</i>

957
00:47:40.583 --> 00:47:43.167
<i>- And I have a surprise for you.</i>
- ["Love the Way" playing]

958
00:47:43.250 --> 00:47:45.667
[imitating drumroll] Ta-da!

959
00:47:46.417 --> 00:47:49.500
The Amur Adonis buds
have finally sprouted.

960
00:47:49.583 --> 00:47:50.875
[chuckling]

961
00:47:50.958 --> 00:47:54.333
Today marks a momentous day
as life has once again sprouted

962
00:47:54.417 --> 00:47:56.042
from this red soil.

963
00:47:56.125 --> 00:47:58.458
Okay, I guess it didn't sprout
from the soil.

964
00:47:58.542 --> 00:48:02.042
Ji-young, another video journal
to your daughter, hmm?

965
00:48:03.125 --> 00:48:04.333
Mm-hmm.

966
00:48:04.417 --> 00:48:07.125
Hi, Nan-young.
I heard you got another rotten tooth.

967
00:48:07.208 --> 00:48:09.833
The news of that even reached Mars.

968
00:48:09.917 --> 00:48:13.542
You have to brush your teeth properly
to become an astronaut.

969
00:48:13.625 --> 00:48:15.167
- [Ji-young laughs]
- Doo-doo-doo.

970
00:48:15.250 --> 00:48:17.708
Do we have a tooth-brushing regulation?

971
00:48:17.792 --> 00:48:19.917
Shush! Just tell her that we have one.

972
00:48:20.000 --> 00:48:20.917
[laughs]

973
00:48:21.000 --> 00:48:22.542
All right. She's right.

974
00:48:23.292 --> 00:48:25.417
You have too many cavities, missy.

975
00:48:25.917 --> 00:48:28.125
Don't forget to brush your teeth
before bed.

976
00:48:28.208 --> 00:48:30.583
And listen to everything your father says.

977
00:48:30.667 --> 00:48:32.625
And eat lots and lots of veggies too!

978
00:48:34.208 --> 00:48:36.375
Don't forget your English studies.

979
00:48:37.250 --> 00:48:38.542
Good night, my darling.

980
00:48:39.292 --> 00:48:41.208
See you in your dreams, hon.

981
00:48:41.792 --> 00:48:44.417
Your mom will haunt your dreams
if you don't brush your teeth!

982
00:48:44.500 --> 00:48:48.292
- Just like how she haunts everyone here.
- Okay. Enough, you guys.

983
00:48:48.375 --> 00:48:49.792
- [rumbling]
- [alarm sounding]

984
00:48:51.042 --> 00:48:52.125
Oh my.

985
00:48:53.333 --> 00:48:54.875
[man] There's an unexpected vibration.

986
00:48:54.958 --> 00:48:57.500
- [woman] We need to get out quickly!
- [yells]

987
00:48:58.000 --> 00:49:00.042
[woman 2] Ji-young! Hurry!

988
00:49:00.625 --> 00:49:01.667
[crashing]

989
00:49:04.167 --> 00:49:05.417
[yelling]

990
00:49:05.500 --> 00:49:06.417
[silence]

991
00:49:06.500 --> 00:49:08.500
- [alarm beeping]
- [Ji-young cries out]

992
00:49:13.000 --> 00:49:15.000
- [explosion rumbles]
- [Ji-young yells]

993
00:49:15.500 --> 00:49:17.500
[tense music playing]

994
00:49:20.167 --> 00:49:21.250
[gasps]

995
00:49:23.792 --> 00:49:26.000
[continues gasping]

996
00:49:36.542 --> 00:49:38.583
- [watch ringing]
- Isn't that that woman?

997
00:49:47.250 --> 00:49:48.417
[ringing stops]

998
00:49:49.792 --> 00:49:50.917
[gasps]

999
00:49:51.542 --> 00:49:52.958
Oh! [Gasps]

1000
00:49:53.625 --> 00:49:59.292
DR. JOO NAN-YOUNG SELECTED AS A MEMBER
OF THE FOURTH MARS EXPEDITION TEAM

1001
00:50:07.292 --> 00:50:09.292
[no audible dialogue]

1002
00:50:14.000 --> 00:50:15.083
[door opens]

1003
00:50:18.500 --> 00:50:21.458
Why are you sitting in the dark?
Why didn't you call me?

1004
00:50:24.000 --> 00:50:26.583
Oh, right, you did. I didn't answer.

1005
00:50:27.208 --> 00:50:28.500
Sorry, I was just swamped.

1006
00:50:29.625 --> 00:50:32.667
Oh, you tidied up. Thanks.

1007
00:50:35.667 --> 00:50:36.667
Jay?

1008
00:50:38.542 --> 00:50:40.125
When were you going to tell me?

1009
00:50:43.625 --> 00:50:44.625
Now.

1010
00:50:47.042 --> 00:50:48.167
When did you find out?

1011
00:50:49.417 --> 00:50:50.833
[Nan-young] A few days ago.

1012
00:50:50.917 --> 00:50:52.083
[scoffs]

1013
00:50:52.167 --> 00:50:53.167
Let me guess…

1014
00:50:54.042 --> 00:50:55.708
The night I was on stage?

1015
00:50:59.208 --> 00:51:00.208
Mm.

1016
00:51:00.833 --> 00:51:01.833
[Jay] You…

1017
00:51:04.000 --> 00:51:05.333
So this was your secret?

1018
00:51:06.167 --> 00:51:07.750
I'm sorry, Jay.

1019
00:51:07.833 --> 00:51:09.125
I had no choice.

1020
00:51:09.917 --> 00:51:11.877
[scoffs] We couldn't tell anyone.
Not even family.

1021
00:51:11.917 --> 00:51:13.542
Speaking of family,

1022
00:51:15.083 --> 00:51:17.417
does your father know
what you're about to do?

1023
00:51:18.583 --> 00:51:20.292
[scoffs] Even if I told him, he wouldn't...

1024
00:51:20.375 --> 00:51:23.208
Well, you should tell him anyway.
You should've told him in advance!

1025
00:51:23.292 --> 00:51:24.292
- Jay.
- [screen beeps]

1026
00:51:27.208 --> 00:51:28.708
Aren't you happy for me?

1027
00:51:29.625 --> 00:51:31.667
I've literally worked my whole life
for this.

1028
00:51:31.750 --> 00:51:33.958
- You know that.
- I know, of course.

1029
00:51:34.458 --> 00:51:36.375
At least I thought I did.

1030
00:51:36.458 --> 00:51:39.250
I guess maybe I convinced myself
that it wasn't what you wanted.

1031
00:51:39.333 --> 00:51:40.667
Yet, there I was,

1032
00:51:40.750 --> 00:51:43.917
blindly encouraging my girlfriend
to go running toward disaster?

1033
00:51:47.292 --> 00:51:48.542
Jay.

1034
00:51:48.625 --> 00:51:50.125
Stay with me.

1035
00:51:52.208 --> 00:51:54.083
[poignant music playing]

1036
00:51:55.792 --> 00:51:58.542
- You could die if you go.
- [Nan-young exhales]

1037
00:52:02.083 --> 00:52:03.958
[voice breaking] Don't do this, Jay.

1038
00:52:07.750 --> 00:52:08.750
Uh…

1039
00:52:09.250 --> 00:52:11.333
Did you go through my things?

1040
00:52:12.500 --> 00:52:14.792
Is that what you're focusing on right now?

1041
00:52:14.875 --> 00:52:17.708
I can't just watch you march
to your death.

1042
00:52:17.792 --> 00:52:20.000
What you saw was a worst-case scenario!

1043
00:52:20.083 --> 00:52:22.500
And that will never happen to me,
I promise!

1044
00:52:22.583 --> 00:52:25.768
You must think I'm an idiot 'cause clearly
you're gonna find a way to justify it.

1045
00:52:25.792 --> 00:52:29.542
This is why I couldn't tell you.
You're not at all like my father.

1046
00:52:29.625 --> 00:52:31.292
You want me to be like your dad?

1047
00:52:31.375 --> 00:52:34.042
Staring up at the sky,
sending messages into the void,

1048
00:52:34.125 --> 00:52:35.917
hoping she'll come back?

1049
00:52:37.667 --> 00:52:39.667
[breathes shakily]

1050
00:52:42.083 --> 00:52:44.458
All right then. I get it.

1051
00:52:48.583 --> 00:52:50.292
We should just end this.

1052
00:52:53.083 --> 00:52:54.083
[Jay exhales]

1053
00:53:00.042 --> 00:53:01.042
How…

1054
00:53:03.125 --> 00:53:04.542
How can you be so cruel?

1055
00:53:14.042 --> 00:53:15.042
[door closes]

1056
00:53:15.625 --> 00:53:17.458
[crying]

1057
00:53:27.792 --> 00:53:30.458
NAN-YOUNG'S

1058
00:53:32.625 --> 00:53:35.125
[continues crying]

1059
00:53:43.875 --> 00:53:46.792
<i>♪ Even though ♪</i>

1060
00:53:46.875 --> 00:53:49.792
<i>♪ You were right beside me ♪</i>

1061
00:53:50.375 --> 00:53:53.000
<i>♪ I still missed you ♪</i>

1062
00:53:53.875 --> 00:53:55.458
<i>♪ Like you're not around… ♪</i>

1063
00:53:55.542 --> 00:53:57.875
[Nan-young] <i>Dad, I'm going to Mars.</i>

1064
00:53:59.417 --> 00:54:02.417
<i>Now I know how hard
this must have been for Mom.</i>

1065
00:54:03.542 --> 00:54:06.083
I bet she's in orbit right about now.

1066
00:54:06.167 --> 00:54:08.542
[caregiver] Come on, sir.
Move away from the window.

1067
00:54:13.250 --> 00:54:16.333
<i>♪ Count all the moons ♪</i>

1068
00:54:16.417 --> 00:54:21.333
<i>♪ Till we see each other again ♪</i>

1069
00:54:26.792 --> 00:54:31.792
<i>♪ I keep singing and singing ♪</i>

1070
00:54:33.458 --> 00:54:36.208
<i>♪ Though I know… ♪</i>

1071
00:54:36.292 --> 00:54:38.667
[Nan-young] <i>But you know</i>
<i>what the worst part is?</i>

1072
00:54:40.792 --> 00:54:43.917
[announcement] <i>The 2:45</i>
<i>American Airlines flight…</i>

1073
00:54:44.000 --> 00:54:45.917
DELETE JAY'S NUMBER?
CONFIRM

1074
00:54:46.000 --> 00:54:48.875
[Nan-young] <i>I finally understand Mom</i>
<i>for the first time.</i>

1075
00:54:49.417 --> 00:54:51.208
<i>Cruel irony.</i>

1076
00:54:51.292 --> 00:54:52.417
[song fades]

1077
00:54:53.417 --> 00:54:54.958
[airplane taking off]

1078
00:55:05.042 --> 00:55:06.042
Hmm.

1079
00:55:11.333 --> 00:55:12.333
Huh?

1080
00:55:17.375 --> 00:55:18.833
[train rumbling]

1081
00:55:24.417 --> 00:55:25.750
[captain] <i>We humans,</i>

1082
00:55:25.833 --> 00:55:28.375
<i>arguably the weakest life-form on Earth,</i>

1083
00:55:28.458 --> 00:55:31.333
<i>have fought, struggled,
and innovated for our survival.</i>

1084
00:55:31.917 --> 00:55:34.875
We've discovered
new continents across the seas,

1085
00:55:35.625 --> 00:55:37.458
yet we've always dreamt of more.

1086
00:55:37.542 --> 00:55:39.000
[camera shutters clicking]

1087
00:55:39.083 --> 00:55:40.167
And now,

1088
00:55:40.250 --> 00:55:43.542
we seek to create
a space-faring civilization

1089
00:55:43.625 --> 00:55:44.917
beyond this blue planet.

1090
00:55:46.417 --> 00:55:50.917
The six-member crew standing here are
pioneers embarking on a great journey…

1091
00:55:51.000 --> 00:55:53.375
[camera shutters clicking]

1092
00:55:53.458 --> 00:55:54.958
[gasps]

1093
00:55:55.917 --> 00:55:57.708
[Rosa] Nans. You okay?

1094
00:55:59.292 --> 00:56:01.208
- Was it a nightmare?
- Huh?

1095
00:56:02.125 --> 00:56:04.250
- Mm-mm.
- [Rosa] You startled me.

1096
00:56:04.333 --> 00:56:05.667
[Nan-young sighs]

1097
00:56:06.542 --> 00:56:09.458
Sheesh, it smells like a locker room
in here, girl. Oh!

1098
00:56:09.958 --> 00:56:12.292
Let's get some air.
It's really beautiful outside!

1099
00:56:12.375 --> 00:56:13.750
Rosa, what are you…

1100
00:56:13.833 --> 00:56:17.042
Go on. Look. Ain't the weather handsome?

1101
00:56:17.958 --> 00:56:19.000
[Nan-young] Huh?

1102
00:56:19.583 --> 00:56:20.583
[sighs]

1103
00:56:22.125 --> 00:56:23.125
Oh.

1104
00:56:23.792 --> 00:56:24.792
Hmm.

1105
00:56:26.708 --> 00:56:27.875
[chuckles]

1106
00:56:27.958 --> 00:56:30.118
- [mom] All right, everyone! Grab a hand.
- [girl] Mommy.

1107
00:56:30.167 --> 00:56:32.500
- [mom] Watch your step.
- [girl] Are we finally ready?

1108
00:56:33.833 --> 00:56:37.000
[laughs] Jay, the tide!

1109
00:56:37.083 --> 00:56:39.208
[laughs]

1110
00:56:39.292 --> 00:56:40.125
[Jay exclaims]

1111
00:56:40.208 --> 00:56:42.208
[both laugh]

1112
00:56:43.083 --> 00:56:44.583
[Nan-young screams playfully]

1113
00:56:45.667 --> 00:56:47.833
[poignant music playing]

1114
00:56:47.917 --> 00:56:49.708
[Jay] <i>Hey, Nan-young.</i>

1115
00:56:51.000 --> 00:56:52.875
<i>You have a pretty shitty boyfriend.</i>

1116
00:56:52.958 --> 00:56:54.667
[Nan-young] <i>You're just figuring that out?</i>

1117
00:56:54.750 --> 00:56:57.417
[Jay] <i>No style to speak of,</i>
<i>no money at all.</i>

1118
00:56:58.167 --> 00:57:01.542
And not an inkling of patience,
which is why he's here.

1119
00:57:01.625 --> 00:57:02.625
I'm glad.

1120
00:57:03.625 --> 00:57:04.833
Makes me like you more.

1121
00:57:05.625 --> 00:57:07.458
- Imperfect Jay.
- [Jay chuckles]

1122
00:57:08.542 --> 00:57:10.042
You've got weird taste.

1123
00:57:10.792 --> 00:57:11.792
[Nan-young] And you?

1124
00:57:12.542 --> 00:57:14.333
Do you wish we'd never met?

1125
00:57:14.958 --> 00:57:15.958
No.

1126
00:57:16.792 --> 00:57:17.958
Not at all.

1127
00:57:19.250 --> 00:57:21.333
The best thing that's ever happened to me

1128
00:57:21.833 --> 00:57:23.000
was meeting you.

1129
00:57:23.083 --> 00:57:25.375
[laughs] Stop it, liar.

1130
00:57:25.458 --> 00:57:27.667
[Jay laughs] I mean it. Really.

1131
00:57:28.750 --> 00:57:29.958
If I'm being honest,

1132
00:57:31.500 --> 00:57:33.333
I'm still not fully on board.

1133
00:57:34.917 --> 00:57:36.667
It's hard for me to support this.

1134
00:57:39.250 --> 00:57:40.458
Make it home safe.

1135
00:57:41.167 --> 00:57:42.500
[music intensifies]

1136
00:57:43.375 --> 00:57:44.792
<i>Come back to me.</i>

1137
00:57:46.042 --> 00:57:47.417
<i>I beg you.</i>

1138
00:57:48.417 --> 00:57:51.333
[Nan-young] <i>I'm sorry</i>
<i>for only thinking of myself.</i>

1139
00:57:52.167 --> 00:57:53.667
[instruments beeping]

1140
00:57:54.667 --> 00:57:56.583
[NASA officer] <i>Countdown T-minus ten.</i>

1141
00:57:57.083 --> 00:58:00.500
- [Jay] <i>For now, just think about yourself.</i>
- [NASA officer] <i>Seven. Six. Five…</i>

1142
00:58:00.583 --> 00:58:03.750
[Jay] <i>You have to be selfish for me</i>
<i>until you get back.</i>

1143
00:58:03.833 --> 00:58:05.792
- [NASA officer] <i>Two. One.</i>
- [engines blasting]

1144
00:58:05.875 --> 00:58:08.958
- [Jay] <i>Try not to do anything dangerous.</i>
- [NASA officer] <i>Zero.</i>

1145
00:58:09.042 --> 00:58:11.083
[Jay] <i>Protect yourself at all costs.</i>

1146
00:58:12.583 --> 00:58:14.333
<i>Promise me, Nan-young.</i>

1147
00:58:14.417 --> 00:58:17.500
Tell me, above all, you'll be safe.

1148
00:58:23.292 --> 00:58:24.333
[Nan-young] I will.

1149
00:58:26.708 --> 00:58:27.917
I promise.

1150
00:58:32.583 --> 00:58:34.750
[rocket blasting]

1151
00:58:34.833 --> 00:58:36.625
[NASA officer] <i>Lift-off confirmed.</i>

1152
00:58:36.708 --> 00:58:39.833
<i>The Seed-1 is slowly
lifting off the launchpad.</i>

1153
00:58:40.583 --> 00:58:42.792
<i>The engines are igniting beautifully.</i>

1154
00:58:42.875 --> 00:58:43.875
<i>Seed-1.</i>

1155
00:58:44.375 --> 00:58:46.792
<i>The first-stage separation in three,</i>

1156
00:58:47.375 --> 00:58:49.625
<i>two, one.</i>

1157
00:58:49.708 --> 00:58:50.708
[grunts]

1158
00:59:13.458 --> 00:59:14.875
[music fades]

1159
00:59:14.958 --> 00:59:16.292
[crowd chattering]

1160
00:59:16.375 --> 00:59:18.495
- [NASA officer] <i>Seed-I left Earth's orbit…</i>
- Excuse me.

1161
00:59:18.542 --> 00:59:20.292
<i>…and is heading toward Mars.</i>

1162
00:59:20.375 --> 00:59:23.083
<i>Finally, a great leap for mankind</i>

1163
00:59:23.167 --> 00:59:24.833
<i>is made once again.</i>

1164
00:59:24.917 --> 00:59:26.917
[crowd cheering and clapping]

1165
00:59:27.833 --> 00:59:29.833
[man] Whoa! What a sight!

1166
00:59:33.125 --> 00:59:34.167
[Jay] Hmm.

1167
00:59:38.333 --> 00:59:39.833
[engines rumbling]

1168
00:59:41.333 --> 00:59:44.083
["Heart to Heart" playing]

1169
00:59:44.667 --> 00:59:45.833
[beeping]

1170
00:59:47.417 --> 00:59:49.917
[woman singing in Korean]

1171
01:00:04.792 --> 01:00:06.792
[inaudible]

1172
01:00:10.958 --> 01:00:12.958
[song continues]

1173
01:00:18.333 --> 01:00:19.917
[inaudible]

1174
01:00:38.083 --> 01:00:40.083
[song continues]

1175
01:00:53.958 --> 01:00:56.792
[Jay] <i>Nan-young, you've inspired me.</i>

1176
01:00:58.375 --> 01:01:00.458
<i>I want to move forward like you.</i>

1177
01:01:02.583 --> 01:01:03.708
<i>Both for myself</i>

1178
01:01:04.875 --> 01:01:05.875
<i>but also</i>

1179
01:01:07.167 --> 01:01:08.167
<i>for you too.</i>

1180
01:01:12.000 --> 01:01:14.000
[song continues]

1181
01:01:24.458 --> 01:01:26.667
<i>♪ You're from another world ♪</i>

1182
01:01:27.167 --> 01:01:32.083
<i>♪ I can feel, I can feel
Somewhere bigger than my star ♪</i>

1183
01:01:32.167 --> 01:01:38.042
<i>♪ Tell me your Sega
Name of your neighbor galaxy… ♪</i>

1184
01:01:38.625 --> 01:01:40.000
[Jay] <i>I finally finished it.</i>

1185
01:01:41.125 --> 01:01:42.542
<i>As my number one fan,</i>

1186
01:01:43.500 --> 01:01:46.000
<i>I thought that
you should hear my song first.</i>

1187
01:01:46.708 --> 01:01:47.708
<i>After all,</i>

1188
01:01:48.417 --> 01:01:51.208
<i>it's your opinion that matters most to me.</i>

1189
01:01:52.167 --> 01:01:53.167
[Jay exhales]

1190
01:01:53.250 --> 01:01:54.167
[man] Hmm. It's good.

1191
01:01:54.250 --> 01:01:56.625
Guess the original songwriter
would know what's best.

1192
01:01:56.708 --> 01:01:59.667
- Ending's not half bad either.
- Di-a, let's set up a session.

1193
01:01:59.750 --> 01:02:02.458
- This'll be a great fit for the album.
- On one condition.

1194
01:02:02.542 --> 01:02:04.125
- Huh?
- And what's that?

1195
01:02:05.542 --> 01:02:08.542
I wanna sing it… live on stage.

1196
01:02:09.375 --> 01:02:10.458
[scoffs]

1197
01:02:12.375 --> 01:02:14.708
IT'S FINALLY DONE!
I WANTED YOU TO HEAR IT FIRST.

1198
01:02:14.792 --> 01:02:17.625
[man] I've finally found my true calling.
Farming!

1199
01:02:17.708 --> 01:02:18.708
[Nan-young] Mm.

1200
01:02:19.792 --> 01:02:21.292
<i>Jay, it's me.</i>

1201
01:02:22.417 --> 01:02:24.375
<i>Our signal strength was good this morning.</i>

1202
01:02:25.292 --> 01:02:27.708
<i>So I rushed to the terminal
as fast as I could,</i>

1203
01:02:28.208 --> 01:02:30.500
<i>and your song
finally finished transferring.</i>

1204
01:02:32.333 --> 01:02:35.833
- "['Bon Voyage" plays through headphones]
<i>- ♪ I lose myself to fun… ♪</i>

1205
01:02:36.417 --> 01:02:37.457
[Nan-young exhales softly]

1206
01:02:38.125 --> 01:02:39.292
<i>You've finished it.</i>

1207
01:02:39.792 --> 01:02:42.375
<i>♪ Drifting to the unknown ♪</i>

1208
01:02:47.125 --> 01:02:49.792
<i>♪ Sleeping somewhere in between… ♪</i>

1209
01:02:51.333 --> 01:02:52.583
[Nan-young sobs]

1210
01:02:55.417 --> 01:02:57.417
[poignant music playing]

1211
01:03:11.750 --> 01:03:13.583
<i>All I could think about while I listened…</i>

1212
01:03:13.667 --> 01:03:15.042
[sobbing continues]

1213
01:03:15.958 --> 01:03:17.625
<i>…was how much I miss you…</i>

1214
01:03:20.292 --> 01:03:22.292
[inaudible]

1215
01:03:23.583 --> 01:03:25.542
<i>…and that I'm not there to console you.</i>

1216
01:03:26.417 --> 01:03:29.958
<i>That loneliness, it must be so painful.</i>

1217
01:03:32.375 --> 01:03:33.875
<i>I'm so sorry for that.</i>

1218
01:03:49.542 --> 01:03:51.125
<i>We'll be arriving on Mars soon,</i>

1219
01:03:51.917 --> 01:03:55.375
<i>which means we probably won't be able
to reach each other for a while.</i>

1220
01:03:55.875 --> 01:03:57.417
<i>But always remember, Jay,</i>

1221
01:03:58.500 --> 01:04:00.208
<i>out there in the starlight,</i>

1222
01:04:00.917 --> 01:04:02.583
<i>someone's cheering you on.</i>

1223
01:04:03.250 --> 01:04:04.917
<i>Your biggest fan.</i>

1224
01:04:05.000 --> 01:04:07.000
[triumphant music playing]

1225
01:04:09.958 --> 01:04:11.958
[engines rumbling]

1226
01:04:40.208 --> 01:04:42.167
[music decreases in intensity]

1227
01:04:43.625 --> 01:04:45.625
[detector trilling]

1228
01:05:03.625 --> 01:05:04.875
[beep]

1229
01:05:21.208 --> 01:05:22.500
[music fades]

1230
01:05:22.583 --> 01:05:23.917
Stay strong, Jay.

1231
01:05:24.875 --> 01:05:25.875
[beep]

1232
01:05:27.958 --> 01:05:30.833
- Someone play some sweet music for us.
- [grunting]

1233
01:05:30.917 --> 01:05:31.792
[beep]

1234
01:05:31.875 --> 01:05:33.417
<i>♪ I lose myself to fun… ♪</i>

1235
01:05:33.500 --> 01:05:35.458
[man] That song? Again?

1236
01:05:36.042 --> 01:05:38.583
[groans] I left
my loved ones behind too, you know!

1237
01:05:38.667 --> 01:05:39.833
[Rosa] Leave 'em alone.

1238
01:05:39.917 --> 01:05:42.750
I'm just giving them a break
until they fix the antennas.

1239
01:05:43.250 --> 01:05:45.850
- [man] I know all the words to this song.
- [Rosa] Me too. [Grunts]

1240
01:05:46.625 --> 01:05:48.625
[detector trills]

1241
01:05:50.792 --> 01:05:51.875
<i>Detected.</i>

1242
01:05:51.958 --> 01:05:53.958
[Nan-young breathes heavily]

1243
01:05:58.583 --> 01:05:59.583
<i>Object found.</i>

1244
01:06:00.458 --> 01:06:02.458
[detector trilling]

1245
01:06:02.542 --> 01:06:04.542
[tense music playing]

1246
01:06:10.333 --> 01:06:12.458
Captain, Joo just found
the abandoned rover

1247
01:06:12.542 --> 01:06:13.750
from the second expedition.

1248
01:06:13.833 --> 01:06:14.833
Did she?

1249
01:06:14.917 --> 01:06:17.542
I'd like to get your permission
to retrieve the rover by myself.

1250
01:06:17.625 --> 01:06:20.333
Looks like that'll be
a two-hour round trip.

1251
01:06:20.417 --> 01:06:21.792
Yes. It's not far.

1252
01:06:21.875 --> 01:06:24.417
- Very well. Permission granted.
- Thank you, Captain.

1253
01:06:24.500 --> 01:06:27.458
Want me to come? I don't like the idea
of you going off alone.

1254
01:06:27.542 --> 01:06:30.042
[chuckles] Don't worry.
I'll be back before lunch.

1255
01:06:30.125 --> 01:06:33.167
Actually, would you mind heating up
my lunch kit too?

1256
01:06:33.250 --> 01:06:35.958
- I'm sure I'll be hungry.
- [Rosa] I'm already hungry. Don't be late.

1257
01:06:36.042 --> 01:06:37.208
[Nan-young] <i>Yes, ma'am.</i>

1258
01:06:37.292 --> 01:06:39.292
[wheels screeching]

1259
01:06:43.125 --> 01:06:45.125
[wind whistling]

1260
01:06:48.333 --> 01:06:49.333
[sighs]

1261
01:06:50.083 --> 01:06:51.458
Oh.

1262
01:06:51.542 --> 01:06:52.542
Uh…

1263
01:06:54.792 --> 01:06:56.583
- [sighs]
- [watch beeps]

1264
01:06:58.667 --> 01:06:59.667
Ah.

1265
01:07:02.792 --> 01:07:04.000
[door opens]

1266
01:07:04.083 --> 01:07:05.292
[Di-a] At it again, huh?

1267
01:07:06.125 --> 01:07:07.542
It's early. What do you want?

1268
01:07:08.292 --> 01:07:12.375
- This is your wake-up call for rehearsal.
- Yeah, yeah. I won't be late.

1269
01:07:14.500 --> 01:07:15.542
[sighs]

1270
01:07:18.250 --> 01:07:20.875
I found your in-ear monitors in my stuff.

1271
01:07:20.958 --> 01:07:21.958
[sighs]

1272
01:07:24.500 --> 01:07:25.500
[Di-a] Come on, Jay.

1273
01:07:27.208 --> 01:07:29.500
Try singing. In front of me.

1274
01:07:34.000 --> 01:07:35.042
[Jay sighs]

1275
01:07:42.250 --> 01:07:44.250
[engine whirring]

1276
01:07:48.292 --> 01:07:50.250
[Nan-young breathing heavily]

1277
01:07:51.625 --> 01:07:53.625
[inquisitive music playing]

1278
01:07:58.333 --> 01:07:59.958
The battery's dead.

1279
01:08:03.167 --> 01:08:05.708
[machinery whirring]

1280
01:08:06.958 --> 01:08:08.583
HQ, this is Joo.

1281
01:08:08.667 --> 01:08:11.250
Endurance rover seems stuck in the sand.

1282
01:08:11.333 --> 01:08:13.583
Requesting additional vehicle support.

1283
01:08:13.667 --> 01:08:15.708
- [radio static]
- HQ, do you copy?

1284
01:08:16.583 --> 01:08:17.583
[detector] <i>Target.</i>

1285
01:08:21.667 --> 01:08:23.208
[detector beeps] <i>Life trace.</i>

1286
01:08:33.750 --> 01:08:35.750
[trilling]

1287
01:08:41.042 --> 01:08:42.042
- HQ.
- [radio static]

1288
01:08:42.125 --> 01:08:43.125
HQ?

1289
01:08:47.000 --> 01:08:48.750
Suit, begin recording.

1290
01:08:48.833 --> 01:08:51.917
Comms are unstable.
Switching to log-based report.

1291
01:08:52.000 --> 01:08:54.750
Biomarkers have been detected
and are within 500 meters.

1292
01:08:54.833 --> 01:08:57.208
I'll examine the results
then head back to base.

1293
01:08:57.292 --> 01:08:59.333
[instruments playing]

1294
01:08:59.417 --> 01:09:02.250
- [man 1] Over here!
- [man 2] Sound check for drums first.

1295
01:09:02.333 --> 01:09:04.417
- [instruments playing]
- [crowd cheering]

1296
01:09:05.292 --> 01:09:07.292
[crowd chattering]

1297
01:09:09.208 --> 01:09:13.042
- [man 3] Di-a. In-ear monitors sound good?
- Uh, yeah, they sound good.

1298
01:09:13.125 --> 01:09:16.583
- [man 3] In-ears are good to go!
- But I think we can bump the vocals.

1299
01:09:16.667 --> 01:09:19.333
- [man 3] Turn up the vocals in her ears.
- [Jay] Hmm.

1300
01:09:19.417 --> 01:09:21.417
[mellow music playing]

1301
01:09:25.208 --> 01:09:26.333
- [Di-a] Jay!
- Huh?

1302
01:09:26.417 --> 01:09:29.000
[Di-a] Get with it!
That's where you're supposed to come in.

1303
01:09:29.083 --> 01:09:30.167
Oh, yeah.

1304
01:09:31.042 --> 01:09:32.792
- Sorry.
- [Di-a] This is our big chance.

1305
01:09:32.875 --> 01:09:34.625
Sorry, everyone.
Let's take it from the top.

1306
01:09:34.708 --> 01:09:36.833
[man] We'll go through
the rehearsal once more.

1307
01:09:36.917 --> 01:09:38.917
[engine revving]

1308
01:09:41.042 --> 01:09:44.500
[suit] <i>Fifty meters ahead.</i>
<i>Crater cliff. Be aware.</i>

1309
01:09:44.583 --> 01:09:46.583
[tense music playing]

1310
01:09:51.375 --> 01:09:55.333
[Nan-young] A meteor impact seems
to have exposed an underground lava cave.

1311
01:09:55.417 --> 01:09:57.708
[breathing heavily]

1312
01:09:57.792 --> 01:09:59.250
[detector trills]

1313
01:09:59.333 --> 01:10:01.292
<i>- Tracing route.</i>
- [Nan-young] Huh?

1314
01:10:01.375 --> 01:10:02.417
[whirring]

1315
01:10:05.167 --> 01:10:07.250
- [detector] <i>Route found.</i>
- [Nan-young exhales sharply]

1316
01:10:12.375 --> 01:10:13.667
[exhales]

1317
01:10:13.750 --> 01:10:14.833
[grunts]

1318
01:10:18.125 --> 01:10:21.167
[grunting, heavy breathing]

1319
01:10:23.375 --> 01:10:25.375
Captain, a tornado signal
has been detected

1320
01:10:25.458 --> 01:10:27.917
in the eastern part of the Arcadia Plains.

1321
01:10:28.500 --> 01:10:30.583
[captain] <i>We had a briefing</i>
<i>about this last night.</i>

1322
01:10:30.667 --> 01:10:33.143
[man] <i>The EF strength has been rapidly</i>
<i>and aggressively growing</i>

1323
01:10:33.167 --> 01:10:36.417
<i>for the last hour.
Any exterior work in those regions</i>

1324
01:10:36.500 --> 01:10:39.083
<i>will likely be too risky
until tomorrow afternoon.</i>

1325
01:10:39.167 --> 01:10:42.000
[captain] That shouldn't present
any problems. Wait.

1326
01:10:42.083 --> 01:10:44.375
Captain, have you looked outside?

1327
01:10:44.458 --> 01:10:46.083
Rosa, where's Nan-young?

1328
01:10:46.167 --> 01:10:47.887
I've been trying
to establish communication,

1329
01:10:47.917 --> 01:10:49.583
but nothing so far.

1330
01:10:49.667 --> 01:10:51.083
- [captain] Damn it!
- Ugh!

1331
01:10:51.875 --> 01:10:53.292
[wind gusting]

1332
01:10:53.375 --> 01:10:55.500
[Rosa] It looks worse than it is.

1333
01:10:56.417 --> 01:10:57.417
Right?

1334
01:11:03.625 --> 01:11:09.708
♪ <i>Bet you know</i>
<i>All the words to shut me up </i> ♪

1335
01:11:10.583 --> 01:11:12.958
♪ <i>Throw my heart out </i> ♪

1336
01:11:13.833 --> 01:11:15.167
[captain] <i>This is HQ.</i>

1337
01:11:15.250 --> 01:11:16.833
[breaking up] <i>Nan-young… read me?</i>

1338
01:11:18.042 --> 01:11:21.250
- [Rosa] <i>Stand by…</i>
- This is Joo. Do you copy?

1339
01:11:22.208 --> 01:11:24.125
[Rosa breaking up on radio] <i>Joo… copy?</i>

1340
01:11:25.083 --> 01:11:28.375
<i>I don't think she can hear us.
What… what do we do?</i>

1341
01:11:29.042 --> 01:11:31.000
<i>The tornado is heading your way!</i>

1342
01:11:31.083 --> 01:11:32.167
[wind roaring]

1343
01:11:32.750 --> 01:11:33.750
[detector] <i>Tracing route.</i>

1344
01:11:33.833 --> 01:11:35.417
Suit, begin recording.

1345
01:11:35.500 --> 01:11:38.461
I'm entering an unidentified cave
where there are traces of the bio marker.

1346
01:11:38.500 --> 01:11:41.917
[coughs] Radio reception remains weak.
This recording will serve as my report...

1347
01:11:42.000 --> 01:11:44.167
[screams]

1348
01:11:46.208 --> 01:11:48.208
[wind whistling]

1349
01:11:48.292 --> 01:11:50.292
[metal creaking]

1350
01:11:53.417 --> 01:11:55.167
[rope whipping]

1351
01:11:55.250 --> 01:11:57.083
- [crash]
- [Nan-young cries out]

1352
01:11:58.500 --> 01:11:59.875
- [rope whipping]
- [creaking]

1353
01:11:59.958 --> 01:12:02.375
[screams, moans]

1354
01:12:02.458 --> 01:12:04.000
[gasps, cries out]

1355
01:12:04.083 --> 01:12:05.625
[tense music playing]

1356
01:12:06.333 --> 01:12:09.167
♪ <i>I'll let you break my heart… </i> ♪

1357
01:12:09.250 --> 01:12:11.250
[high-pitched squealing]

1358
01:12:12.542 --> 01:12:14.542
[wind roaring]

1359
01:12:17.125 --> 01:12:19.125
[panting]

1360
01:12:20.458 --> 01:12:22.458
[creaking]

1361
01:12:23.625 --> 01:12:24.542
[breathing]

1362
01:12:24.625 --> 01:12:27.042
[beeping]

1363
01:12:30.708 --> 01:12:32.708
[creaking]

1364
01:12:35.167 --> 01:12:37.250
[ominous music playing]

1365
01:12:38.042 --> 01:12:39.542
[creaking]

1366
01:12:42.375 --> 01:12:44.000
[creaking]

1367
01:12:45.417 --> 01:12:47.208
[music builds]

1368
01:12:47.292 --> 01:12:48.292
[string snaps]

1369
01:12:50.583 --> 01:12:52.583
[crash]

1370
01:12:54.125 --> 01:12:56.125
[wind roaring]

1371
01:13:00.708 --> 01:13:03.101
[Di-a] I wrote that last song
when I had a devastating crush.

1372
01:13:03.125 --> 01:13:04.833
- [chuckles]
- [crowd chanting] Di-a! Di-a!

1373
01:13:04.917 --> 01:13:07.708
- That one is called "Moonlight."
- [crowd continues chanting]

1374
01:13:07.792 --> 01:13:10.042
[tense music playing]

1375
01:13:14.958 --> 01:13:16.958
- [Nan-young breathes]
- [alarm beeping]

1376
01:13:22.625 --> 01:13:24.625
[regular breathing continues]

1377
01:13:27.167 --> 01:13:28.375
[music builds, stops]

1378
01:13:28.458 --> 01:13:30.958
- [suit] <i>Alert. Helmet damaged.</i>
- [Nan-young cries out]

1379
01:13:31.042 --> 01:13:33.333
[suit] <i>Oxygen leak detected.</i>

1380
01:13:33.417 --> 01:13:34.667
[panting]

1381
01:13:34.750 --> 01:13:37.542
[suit] <i>Oxygen level, 10.5.</i>

1382
01:13:38.042 --> 01:13:40.125
<i>- 10.1.</i>
- [groans]

1383
01:13:40.208 --> 01:13:42.208
<i>- 9.6.</i>
- [grunting]

1384
01:13:42.292 --> 01:13:44.875
<i>- Alert. Helmet damaged.</i>
- [air hissing]

1385
01:13:44.958 --> 01:13:46.792
<i>- Oxygen leak detected.</i>
- [exclaims]

1386
01:13:47.542 --> 01:13:49.958
<i>- Alert.</i>
- [hissing stops]

1387
01:13:50.042 --> 01:13:52.125
[trilling and beeping]

1388
01:13:52.208 --> 01:13:55.000
[panting]

1389
01:13:58.500 --> 01:14:00.167
[grunts]

1390
01:14:03.292 --> 01:14:04.500
[detector] <i>Life trace.</i>

1391
01:14:06.458 --> 01:14:07.500
<i>Route found.</i>

1392
01:14:09.667 --> 01:14:10.833
[Nan-young coughing]

1393
01:14:10.917 --> 01:14:12.208
[detector] <i>Tracing route.</i>

1394
01:14:12.792 --> 01:14:14.792
[Nan-young grunting]

1395
01:14:19.500 --> 01:14:20.500
[cries out]

1396
01:14:22.625 --> 01:14:24.458
[Rosa] Rover, start engine.

1397
01:14:24.542 --> 01:14:25.958
Open hatch! [Pants]

1398
01:14:26.042 --> 01:14:28.750
Oh no. It seems like
there's an electrical interference

1399
01:14:28.833 --> 01:14:29.917
with the motion sensor.

1400
01:14:30.000 --> 01:14:31.042
[captain] Damn storm.

1401
01:14:31.125 --> 01:14:34.083
- [man] <i>We got something from Nan-young.</i>
- Pull it up on the screen.

1402
01:14:34.167 --> 01:14:36.542
Remaining oxygen is 9.1?

1403
01:14:37.375 --> 01:14:40.083
She can't breathe
because of the air bleeding.

1404
01:14:40.167 --> 01:14:41.417
[panting]

1405
01:14:41.500 --> 01:14:42.833
[grunts]

1406
01:14:42.917 --> 01:14:45.458
We need to go in right now. [Grunts]

1407
01:14:45.542 --> 01:14:48.708
Check Nan-young's last words video.

1408
01:14:48.792 --> 01:14:50.875
Monitor for any confidential information.

1409
01:14:50.958 --> 01:14:55.125
Captain, we can't.
If we don't something now, she'll die!

1410
01:14:55.208 --> 01:14:57.917
She only has ten minutes of air left.

1411
01:14:58.833 --> 01:15:02.000
The origin point of the signal
is two hours from here.

1412
01:15:02.500 --> 01:15:04.792
[Rosa] So what? She's not dead yet.

1413
01:15:05.667 --> 01:15:07.458
We still have ten more minutes!

1414
01:15:07.542 --> 01:15:09.917
[panicked cries] Captain!

1415
01:15:10.000 --> 01:15:11.833
[detector trilling]

1416
01:15:11.917 --> 01:15:14.583
- [suit] <i>Battery power at 15%.</i>
- [Nan-young grunting]

1417
01:15:14.667 --> 01:15:16.583
[suit] <i>Oxygen level at risk.</i>

1418
01:15:17.083 --> 01:15:19.667
<i>- Activating survival mode.</i>
- [Nan-young cries out]

1419
01:15:19.750 --> 01:15:21.375
[suit] <i>Reducing battery power.</i>

1420
01:15:23.125 --> 01:15:24.167
<i>Warning.</i>

1421
01:15:24.250 --> 01:15:26.667
<i>Suit oxygen level at 8%.</i>

1422
01:15:27.292 --> 01:15:28.958
<i>Carbon dioxide filtration…</i>

1423
01:15:29.042 --> 01:15:31.000
- [panicked panting]
- [beeping]

1424
01:15:34.792 --> 01:15:36.000
[Di-a] Ah!

1425
01:15:37.125 --> 01:15:41.000
Thank you for coming out to the showcase
performance of The Moles.

1426
01:15:42.083 --> 01:15:46.167
One last surprise for all the fans
who made the trek to come see us here.

1427
01:15:46.250 --> 01:15:47.333
[crowd cheering]

1428
01:15:47.917 --> 01:15:49.042
Jay!

1429
01:15:52.500 --> 01:15:55.708
- [crowd chanting] Jay! Jay! Jay! Jay!
- [clears throat]

1430
01:15:55.792 --> 01:16:00.500
[crowd continues chanting]
Jay! Jay! Jay! Jay! Jay! Jay!

1431
01:16:00.583 --> 01:16:02.375
[wind whistling]

1432
01:16:06.500 --> 01:16:08.500
[sniffling, whimpers]

1433
01:16:16.917 --> 01:16:19.000
[sobbing]

1434
01:16:25.667 --> 01:16:27.208
<i>Jay. It's me,</i>

1435
01:16:28.083 --> 01:16:29.083
<i>Nan-young.</i>

1436
01:16:29.542 --> 01:16:31.542
- [beeping]
- [breathing heavily]

1437
01:16:35.583 --> 01:16:36.833
<i>When I was a kid,</i>

1438
01:16:36.917 --> 01:16:39.833
<i>I never remembered to carry
an umbrella with me.</i>

1439
01:16:39.917 --> 01:16:41.167
[rain pattering]

1440
01:16:41.250 --> 01:16:43.250
[poignant music playing]

1441
01:16:43.333 --> 01:16:46.042
<i>All the same,
I never seemed to get rained on.</i>

1442
01:16:47.750 --> 01:16:50.167
<i>Dad would always come
to pick me up from school.</i>

1443
01:16:51.250 --> 01:16:53.375
<i>He was always staring up at the sky.</i>

1444
01:16:53.458 --> 01:16:56.333
<i>I guess that gave him a knack
for predicting the weather.</i>

1445
01:16:57.375 --> 01:16:59.458
<i>I kept that habit into adulthood.</i>

1446
01:16:59.958 --> 01:17:02.083
<i>I almost never carry an umbrella with me.</i>

1447
01:17:02.167 --> 01:17:03.625
- [horn honks]
- Ah!

1448
01:17:04.708 --> 01:17:06.792
- [Jay] Oh.
- [Nan-young] <i>But you know what?</i>

1449
01:17:06.875 --> 01:17:08.375
[Jay breathes heavily]

1450
01:17:08.458 --> 01:17:10.299
- [Nan-young] <i>On that day, you know.</i>
- Nan-young.

1451
01:17:10.375 --> 01:17:14.792
[Nan-young] <i>The day you started calling me</i>
<i>by my name. Well, that was…</i>

1452
01:17:15.292 --> 01:17:17.792
[Jay] I can… call you
by your name now, right?

1453
01:17:17.875 --> 01:17:21.125
[Nan-young] <i>It was the first time that</i>
<i>I shared an umbrella since I was a kid.</i>

1454
01:17:21.208 --> 01:17:23.625
[laughing]

1455
01:17:23.708 --> 01:17:26.542
<i>I'm pretty sure
it's also the day that I fell for you.</i>

1456
01:17:26.625 --> 01:17:28.167
[panting]

1457
01:17:30.000 --> 01:17:31.000
<i>Hmm.</i>

1458
01:17:31.708 --> 01:17:34.917
If you're watching this right now,
then it's not good news.

1459
01:17:35.417 --> 01:17:37.042
I imagine it's not pleasant.

1460
01:17:37.542 --> 01:17:38.583
I'm sorry.

1461
01:17:38.667 --> 01:17:40.250
[Nan-young panting in suit]

1462
01:17:40.333 --> 01:17:41.333
Jay,

1463
01:17:42.083 --> 01:17:44.667
I clung to my path in life so tight.

1464
01:17:45.208 --> 01:17:47.375
<i>But then I stumbled down a side road,</i>

1465
01:17:47.458 --> 01:17:53.000
<i>a road I didn't expect at all,
and found there a glittering oasis.</i>

1466
01:17:53.083 --> 01:17:55.083
[Nan-young grunting in suit]

1467
01:17:57.875 --> 01:17:59.625
<i>That's who you are to me, Jay.</i>

1468
01:18:01.333 --> 01:18:05.917
<i>A guide who led me down a road
I didn't even know existed.</i>

1469
01:18:07.375 --> 01:18:09.917
[Nan-young gasping in suit]

1470
01:18:14.875 --> 01:18:16.792
<i>I can't imagine how difficult this is.</i>

1471
01:18:17.667 --> 01:18:18.667
<i>But, Jay…</i>

1472
01:18:20.500 --> 01:18:24.500
<i>Please, try not to be too sad
and try to move on.</i>

1473
01:18:26.042 --> 01:18:28.875
<i>Live without regrets. Be true to yourself.</i>

1474
01:18:29.875 --> 01:18:31.625
[gasping]

1475
01:18:31.708 --> 01:18:33.917
<i>And please, use that voice of yours.</i>

1476
01:18:36.125 --> 01:18:37.917
<i>And have a beautiful life.</i>

1477
01:18:42.292 --> 01:18:43.667
[breathing shakily]

1478
01:18:44.542 --> 01:18:46.958
[gasping softly]

1479
01:18:47.875 --> 01:18:49.292
[exhales]

1480
01:18:49.375 --> 01:18:51.333
I've never seen Jay sing.

1481
01:18:52.958 --> 01:18:55.833
Okay, switch to camera three.
Let's get the wide shot.

1482
01:18:55.917 --> 01:18:59.083
- [man] Can we get a check on mic one?
- [Nan-young] <i>And don't forget, Jay.</i>

1483
01:19:00.917 --> 01:19:02.292
<i>Somewhere in the starlight…</i>

1484
01:19:02.375 --> 01:19:03.458
[laughing]

1485
01:19:03.542 --> 01:19:05.542
…<i>there's someone who's forever and always…</i>

1486
01:19:05.625 --> 01:19:07.167
[laughing]

1487
01:19:07.250 --> 01:19:08.625
<i>…cheering you on.</i>

1488
01:19:09.833 --> 01:19:10.833
[Jay clears throat]

1489
01:19:12.583 --> 01:19:15.458
[singing a cappella]
♪ <i>I lose myself to fun </i> ♪

1490
01:19:18.125 --> 01:19:20.333
<i>♪ In nameless cities ♪</i>

1491
01:19:22.208 --> 01:19:25.458
<i>♪ Drifting to the unknown ♪</i>

1492
01:19:28.958 --> 01:19:32.250
♪ <i>Sleeping somewhere in between </i> ♪

1493
01:19:32.792 --> 01:19:39.292
<i>♪ For someone like me</i>
<i>Life is sometimes just hard to foresee </i> ♪

1494
01:19:41.208 --> 01:19:47.125
<i>♪ Holding my breath</i>
<i>I'll step through concrete mountains </i> ♪

1495
01:19:47.208 --> 01:19:53.958
<i>♪ I'll overcome it all
And wipe the dust off my face ♪</i>

1496
01:19:55.708 --> 01:20:01.750
<i>♪ Many people are caught</i>
<i>Within a question </i> ♪

1497
01:20:01.833 --> 01:20:05.833
<i>♪ In between zero and one is where ♪</i>

1498
01:20:05.917 --> 01:20:09.667
<i>♪ They meet their love ♪</i>

1499
01:20:12.292 --> 01:20:16.500
♪ <i>Beyond the stars </i> ♪

1500
01:20:16.583 --> 01:20:19.167
♪ <i>Have a good ride, bon voyage </i> ♪

1501
01:20:19.250 --> 01:20:23.375
♪ <i>Time doesn't matter </i> ♪

1502
01:20:23.958 --> 01:20:26.167
♪ <i>We're meant for each other </i> ♪

1503
01:20:26.833 --> 01:20:30.458
♪ <i>Although we're far apart </i> ♪

1504
01:20:31.708 --> 01:20:38.542
♪ <i>I'll always find a way to your heart… </i> ♪

1505
01:20:40.042 --> 01:20:42.167
[man] Hey! [Laughs]

1506
01:20:42.792 --> 01:20:45.250
- [Di-a] Hey.
- Enough! Enough already.

1507
01:20:45.917 --> 01:20:49.125
Come on, you guys. I mean, that was
absolutely one of our best shows,

1508
01:20:49.208 --> 01:20:50.125
hands down!

1509
01:20:50.208 --> 01:20:52.208
["Bon Voyage" continues]

1510
01:20:54.333 --> 01:20:56.333
[Jay vocalizing]

1511
01:20:59.958 --> 01:21:00.875
<i>Breaking news.</i>

1512
01:21:00.958 --> 01:21:04.458
<i>NASA has reported that
the Korean national Dr. Joo Nan-young,</i>

1513
01:21:04.542 --> 01:21:08.375
<i>who embarked on a Mars expedition
in November, has gone missing.</i>

1514
01:21:08.458 --> 01:21:11.917
<i>It appears a sudden shift in weather
severed communication lines,</i>

1515
01:21:12.000 --> 01:21:15.750
<i>and Dr. Joo's location has remained
untraceable for over an hour.</i>

1516
01:21:15.833 --> 01:21:20.667
<i>♪ You can lean on me
And always hold me tight… ♪</i>

1517
01:21:20.750 --> 01:21:21.750
[sighs]

1518
01:21:22.750 --> 01:21:25.875
Did she remember her umbrella?

1519
01:21:25.958 --> 01:21:30.500
<i>NASA reports that Dr. Joo went missing
while engaging in an exploratory mission</i>

1520
01:21:30.583 --> 01:21:32.042
<i>of an unidentified lava cave…</i>

1521
01:21:32.125 --> 01:21:35.792
[groans] No! It can't be! No!

1522
01:21:35.875 --> 01:21:37.375
[reporter] <i>NASA continues to…</i>

1523
01:21:37.875 --> 01:21:39.875
<i>♪ Reach my hand out ♪</i>

1524
01:21:39.958 --> 01:21:43.375
♪ <i>And your radiance shines on throughout </i> ♪

1525
01:21:43.458 --> 01:21:47.208
♪ <i>I'll call your name over and over </i> ♪

1526
01:21:47.292 --> 01:21:50.625
- ♪ <i>As loud as I can shout </i> ♪
- [horn honking]

1527
01:21:52.250 --> 01:21:57.875
♪ <i>Now I'm down here</i>
<i>Looking way up to the sky </i> ♪

1528
01:21:57.958 --> 01:22:04.917
<i>♪ Singing to the stars so that
We both can live on as time goes by ♪</i>

1529
01:22:05.000 --> 01:22:06.542
[gasping]

1530
01:22:08.625 --> 01:22:12.708
<i>♪ Beyond the stars ♪</i>

1531
01:22:12.792 --> 01:22:15.792
<i>- ♪ Have a good ride, bon voyage ♪</i>
- Jay.

1532
01:22:15.875 --> 01:22:17.750
[sobbing] I'm scared.

1533
01:22:17.833 --> 01:22:20.125
<i>♪ Time doesn't matter ♪</i>

1534
01:22:20.208 --> 01:22:22.583
<i>♪ We're meant for each other ♪</i>

1535
01:22:23.167 --> 01:22:26.667
<i>♪ Although we're far apart ♪</i>

1536
01:22:28.208 --> 01:22:34.500
<i>♪ I'll always find a way to your heart… ♪</i>

1537
01:22:34.583 --> 01:22:37.542
I need to see Mr. Joo, your patient.
It's about his daughter!

1538
01:22:37.625 --> 01:22:39.167
[Jay grunts]

1539
01:22:39.250 --> 01:22:40.625
- [security] Hey.
- [nurse] Wait!

1540
01:22:40.708 --> 01:22:43.250
[Jay grunts, pants]

1541
01:22:44.000 --> 01:22:45.000
Mr. Joo!

1542
01:22:47.875 --> 01:22:50.875
- Can I… borrow this for a while?
- Why?

1543
01:22:50.958 --> 01:22:52.250
What is it, son?

1544
01:22:52.875 --> 01:22:55.708
Maybe you also have a message to send?

1545
01:22:57.083 --> 01:22:57.958
[Jay] Yeah.

1546
01:22:58.042 --> 01:23:00.042
[Jay vocalizing]

1547
01:23:00.125 --> 01:23:02.125
[Nan-young gasping]

1548
01:23:09.833 --> 01:23:11.625
[grunting]

1549
01:23:12.250 --> 01:23:14.333
["Bon Voyage" ends]

1550
01:23:14.417 --> 01:23:16.500
[gasping]

1551
01:23:21.167 --> 01:23:23.000
Mommy! [Giggles]

1552
01:23:23.083 --> 01:23:26.167
Mommy! [Giggles]

1553
01:23:28.083 --> 01:23:30.042
Nan-young! [Laughs]

1554
01:23:30.875 --> 01:23:32.500
- [Jay] <i>Nan-young.</i>
- There you are.

1555
01:23:33.375 --> 01:23:37.417
[Jay] <i>All I ever wanted</i>
<i>was to surround you with light.</i>

1556
01:23:37.500 --> 01:23:39.101
[father] What should we have for dinner?

1557
01:23:39.125 --> 01:23:40.958
[Ji-young] I don't know.
Maybe we do ramyeon?

1558
01:23:41.042 --> 01:23:42.625
[father] Ramyeon again?

1559
01:23:42.708 --> 01:23:45.000
[Jay] <i>The last thing I wanted you to see</i>

1560
01:23:45.750 --> 01:23:48.417
<i>were the shadows I carry inside.</i>

1561
01:23:49.875 --> 01:23:51.833
<i>How could a nobody like me</i>

1562
01:23:52.417 --> 01:23:55.375
<i>ever dare to want someone
as extraordinary as you?</i>

1563
01:23:56.792 --> 01:23:59.458
<i>I'd tell myself that
I should just put an end to it.</i>

1564
01:24:00.583 --> 01:24:01.833
<i>But in the morning,</i>

1565
01:24:02.583 --> 01:24:04.542
<i>I'd long for those traces of you.</i>

1566
01:24:06.667 --> 01:24:09.000
<i>And in the end, it was you who taught me</i>

1567
01:24:09.542 --> 01:24:12.000
<i>that light and shadow are inseparable.</i>

1568
01:24:13.917 --> 01:24:15.875
<i>And if you don't embrace the shadows,</i>

1569
01:24:16.417 --> 01:24:18.125
<i>then you'll never see the light.</i>

1570
01:24:20.833 --> 01:24:22.583
- [thunder crashing]
- Please! Please work!

1571
01:24:24.000 --> 01:24:25.667
<i>Just waiting indefinitely,</i>

1572
01:24:26.583 --> 01:24:28.792
<i>I won't lie, it hurts.</i>

1573
01:24:28.875 --> 01:24:30.125
<i>Sometimes a lot.</i>

1574
01:24:31.208 --> 01:24:33.458
<i>But if there's one thing I know,</i>

1575
01:24:34.542 --> 01:24:36.958
it's that I can't ever give up on you!

1576
01:24:38.042 --> 01:24:41.333
<i>So don't you dare go giving up on me.</i>

1577
01:24:41.417 --> 01:24:42.500
[Nan-young inhales]

1578
01:24:42.583 --> 01:24:44.417
[Jay] <i>I need you to come back.</i>

1579
01:24:45.000 --> 01:24:46.250
<i>Put an end to this wait</i>

1580
01:24:46.917 --> 01:24:48.375
and save me.

1581
01:24:52.458 --> 01:24:53.958
[gasps]

1582
01:24:56.042 --> 01:24:57.792
[gasping]

1583
01:25:03.083 --> 01:25:07.042
<i>♪ Beyond the stars ♪</i>

1584
01:25:07.542 --> 01:25:10.333
<i>♪ Have a good ride, bon voyage ♪</i>

1585
01:25:10.417 --> 01:25:14.125
<i>- ♪ Time doesn't matter ♪</i>
- Jay!

1586
01:25:14.208 --> 01:25:15.708
[Jay] Sorry for the wait.

1587
01:25:15.792 --> 01:25:17.625
<i>♪ We're meant for each other ♪</i>

1588
01:25:17.708 --> 01:25:21.375
<i>♪ Although we're far apart ♪</i>

1589
01:25:22.667 --> 01:25:26.875
<i>♪ I'll always find a way to your heart… ♪</i>

1590
01:25:26.958 --> 01:25:28.375
[Jay] Crybaby.

1591
01:25:28.458 --> 01:25:31.125
[Nan-young] I'm not. I'm not crying.

1592
01:25:31.208 --> 01:25:32.500
Neither am I.

1593
01:25:32.583 --> 01:25:34.875
[Nan-young sobbing]

1594
01:25:40.000 --> 01:25:41.000
Oh no.

1595
01:25:41.042 --> 01:25:43.125
Please don't! Jay! Don't go!

1596
01:25:43.208 --> 01:25:44.875
[whimpering]

1597
01:25:44.958 --> 01:25:49.167
Don't do this! You can't!
Please don't leave me, Jay! [Cries]

1598
01:25:49.250 --> 01:25:50.250
No!

1599
01:25:50.792 --> 01:25:53.542
I'm begging you! Don't leave me, Jay!

1600
01:25:54.917 --> 01:25:57.917
[sobbing] Jay, please.

1601
01:25:58.833 --> 01:26:00.875
[song ends]

1602
01:26:01.583 --> 01:26:03.167
[beeping]

1603
01:26:04.458 --> 01:26:06.458
[panting]

1604
01:26:27.583 --> 01:26:29.583
[breathing heavily]

1605
01:26:32.417 --> 01:26:33.958
- [grunting]
- [metal squealing]

1606
01:26:34.708 --> 01:26:36.708
[grunting]

1607
01:26:37.333 --> 01:26:38.958
[metal bangs]

1608
01:26:39.958 --> 01:26:41.958
[panting]

1609
01:26:44.250 --> 01:26:46.417
[suit] <i>Main system operating nominally.</i>

1610
01:26:46.917 --> 01:26:48.833
<i>Manual mode activated.</i>

1611
01:26:50.208 --> 01:26:52.750
- [sighs]
- [faint beeping]

1612
01:26:54.042 --> 01:26:55.500
[poignant music playing]

1613
01:27:08.292 --> 01:27:10.292
[beeping continues]

1614
01:27:43.208 --> 01:27:44.208
[sighs]

1615
01:27:45.208 --> 01:27:46.667
[beeping fades]

1616
01:27:50.000 --> 01:27:51.208
[silence]

1617
01:27:52.875 --> 01:27:54.333
[Nan-young] <i>It's warm.</i>

1618
01:27:55.917 --> 01:27:57.917
[breathing faintly]

1619
01:28:02.625 --> 01:28:04.167
[ethereal music playing]

1620
01:28:05.417 --> 01:28:06.875
- [grunts]
- [tapping on glass]

1621
01:28:10.542 --> 01:28:12.542
[Nan-young exhales]

1622
01:28:15.917 --> 01:28:16.917
[inaudible]

1623
01:28:20.875 --> 01:28:22.875
[grunting]

1624
01:28:24.292 --> 01:28:25.292
Mom?

1625
01:28:37.833 --> 01:28:38.917
I love you.

1626
01:28:41.333 --> 01:28:43.333
[cries quietly]

1627
01:28:52.792 --> 01:28:54.958
[Nan-young crying softly]

1628
01:29:12.083 --> 01:29:14.000
- [Nan-young] <i>I made it!</i>
- Oh!

1629
01:29:14.083 --> 01:29:16.667
- Nan… Nan-young.
- [Nan-young sobbing]

1630
01:29:16.750 --> 01:29:18.708
Nan-young! Nan-young! Oh!

1631
01:29:19.625 --> 01:29:20.708
[Nan-young] <i>And also…</i>

1632
01:29:21.292 --> 01:29:23.750
- Nan-young, where are you?
- [Nan-young] <i>I'm alive.</i>

1633
01:29:23.833 --> 01:29:25.542
Can you hear me? Oh.

1634
01:29:25.625 --> 01:29:27.375
[Nan-young] <i>I heard your message.</i>

1635
01:29:28.083 --> 01:29:29.750
[laughs]

1636
01:29:29.833 --> 01:29:31.875
Your voice sounded so unfamiliar.

1637
01:29:33.042 --> 01:29:34.708
Are you Jay? [Laughs]

1638
01:29:36.542 --> 01:29:38.542
[Jay exhales]

1639
01:29:39.542 --> 01:29:43.542
[Nan-young] <i>Maybe it's the distance,</i>
<i>but it feels like a dream.</i>

1640
01:29:43.625 --> 01:29:44.958
[Jay chuckles]

1641
01:29:45.458 --> 01:29:47.500
It's not a dream. Thank goodness.

1642
01:29:49.167 --> 01:29:53.125
[Nan-young] <i>I've come all this way,</i>
<i>and only now I've realized,</i>

1643
01:29:53.208 --> 01:29:54.125
<i>well,</i>

1644
01:29:54.208 --> 01:29:57.125
<i>there's something
I've been meaning to tell you,</i>

1645
01:29:57.208 --> 01:29:58.417
<i>and I'm ready now.</i>

1646
01:30:01.917 --> 01:30:03.333
<i>I love you, Jay.</i>

1647
01:30:04.500 --> 01:30:06.125
[Jay chuckles]

1648
01:30:06.208 --> 01:30:08.208
[both laugh]

1649
01:30:13.083 --> 01:30:14.125
[Rosa] Nan-young!

1650
01:30:14.875 --> 01:30:17.708
Thank goodness.
It's you. It's you! I've found you.

1651
01:30:17.792 --> 01:30:21.125
Over here! She's alive! Oh my goodness!

1652
01:30:21.750 --> 01:30:24.292
[journalist] <i>Hello, everyone,</i>
<i>and welcome to </i>Today in History.

1653
01:30:24.375 --> 01:30:27.917
<i>On this day, Koreans and all the people
of the world were awestruck.</i>

1654
01:30:28.417 --> 01:30:31.917
<i>Not only did the survival
and dramatic rescue of Dr. Joo Nan-young</i>

1655
01:30:32.000 --> 01:30:33.083
<i>hold the world rapt,</i>

1656
01:30:33.167 --> 01:30:35.958
<i>but even more sensational
was the fact that Dr. Joo discovered</i>

1657
01:30:36.042 --> 01:30:40.333
<i>a cultivated garden of Amur Adonis flowers
beneath the martian surface.</i>

1658
01:30:40.417 --> 01:30:43.042
[Nan-young] <i>There are certain things</i>
<i>that you can only realize</i>

1659
01:30:43.125 --> 01:30:44.625
<i>from a great distance.</i>

1660
01:30:46.250 --> 01:30:49.083
<i>Something I'd failed to notice
before I went away.</i>

1661
01:30:49.167 --> 01:30:50.667
[panting]

1662
01:30:50.750 --> 01:30:53.458
<i>Now that I'm back, I treasure it.</i>

1663
01:30:53.542 --> 01:30:55.750
[panting]

1664
01:30:55.833 --> 01:30:58.625
[Nan-young] <i>To think</i>
<i>it had always been right here.</i>

1665
01:31:00.500 --> 01:31:01.708
<i>Beneath my feet.</i>

1666
01:31:01.792 --> 01:31:03.792
[emotional music playing]

1667
01:31:05.667 --> 01:31:07.000
<i>Before my eyes.</i>

1668
01:31:13.083 --> 01:31:14.083
<i>Within us.</i>

1669
01:31:23.292 --> 01:31:24.458
[exhales]

1670
01:31:31.458 --> 01:31:32.458
<i>And even better,</i>

1671
01:31:33.833 --> 01:31:34.833
<i>it's right here</i>

1672
01:31:35.333 --> 01:31:36.333
<i>on this planet.</i>

1673
01:31:38.167 --> 01:31:39.583
["Take Me" playing]

1674
01:31:39.667 --> 01:31:43.708
<i>♪ Take me to another star ♪</i>

1675
01:31:43.792 --> 01:31:45.792
[singing in Korean]

1676
01:31:58.792 --> 01:32:03.083
<i>♪ Take me to another star ♪</i>

1677
01:32:03.167 --> 01:32:05.167
[singing in Korean]

1678
01:32:12.000 --> 01:32:18.208
LOST IN STARLIGHT

1679
01:33:16.333 --> 01:33:18.625
[vocalizing]

1680
01:33:18.708 --> 01:33:21.042
[singing in Korean]

1681
01:33:21.125 --> 01:33:23.125
[vocalizing]

1682
01:33:25.583 --> 01:33:27.583
[singing in Korean]

1683
01:33:34.292 --> 01:33:39.042
<i>♪ Oh, take me to another star ♪</i>

1684
01:33:39.125 --> 01:33:41.125
[singing in Korean]

1685
